docs/IMPLEMENTATION_LOG.md:9032:Fixed the confirmed stale UI result after a failed new query, including late-response navigation protection. Browser verified before/after without changing baseline scores. Local harness timestamp/plan-ID mistakes failed before inference; retained logs/new corrected plan. No Jev retries.
docs/IMPLEMENTATION_LOG.md:9034:Cost: **22 new DeepSeek calls** (2 extraction, 3 reconciliation, 17 narrative/constraint), all with usage; low/peak **$0.052482306 / $0.104964612**, all in weekday peak windows. No truncations; one reconciliation schema recovery. Cumulative **294 calls**, known interval **$0.621766404–$1.240096914** plus old Jev unresolved reserve **$0.001931286**. No budget increase. Data, coding/judging labor and infrastructure unmetered. [Delta](../evals/q2-cost-delta-2026-09-23.json).
docs/IMPLEMENTATION_LOG.md:9040:Continued after the user's “继续”. Used three already archived sources, with 17 predeclared diagnostic opportunities; no new TN/data fetch. Added 44 reviewed claims (including three explicit same-packet amendments), three amended Apple theses, 14 assessments and five changes. Current real ledger: 27 / 205 / 22 / 78 / 25 for source/claim/thesis/evaluation/change. The NHTSA proposal was withheld and FTC notification remained background. Source windows increased from 4.74% to 7.08%; this is not recall.
docs/IMPLEMENTATION_LOG.md:9044:**Costs:** 92 requests this slice: extraction 35 ($0.110951460 peak), reconciliation 9 ($0.175642032), narrative development/recovery 44 ($0.199787676), Jev 4 (HTTP 403, usage unknown). Known token total $0.243190584–$0.486381168; all 88 completed requests fell in weekday peak windows, so use $0.486381168 conservatively. Includes 12 truncations and all unsuccessful/development attempts. Four Jev requests retain $0.001931286 reservation; no automatic retry or assumed zero invoice. Unchanged stage allocations total $8. Cumulative 272 requests, known-price interval $0.569284098–$1.135132302 plus unknown reservation. [Cost delta](../evals/q1-cost-delta-2026-09-23.json), [raw audit](../evals/history/usage-audits-2026-09-22-23/q1-2026-09-23-usage-audit.json). Coding/semantic-review labor and data/storage/tax remain unmetered.
docs/IMPLEMENTATION_LOG.md:9046:**Audit correction:** an intermediate local report wrongly counted Jev failures as agreement. Corrected status-aware summary yields 62/78 judged, 60 compatible, two prior reviewed disagreements, 16 unjudged. Use [v2 research report](../evals/q1-research-review-2026-09-23-v2.json); v1 is explicitly superseded. A failed test during development expected an integer where ledger.report returns a call list; the assertion was corrected without changing ledger behavior.
docs/IMPLEMENTATION_LOG.md:9048:**Validation:** 256 tests, both demos, 309 context snapshots, whole-ledger quote/dependency checks, final five query cache replays, 22-card desktop/mobile and historical browser checks. Final five queries are explicitly agent-reviewed development examples, not held-out gold. The live workbench stays at 8788; test Chrome stopped. Independent human labels, broader corpus/scale, Jev access restoration and multiday acceptance remain pending. [Code review](history/CODE_REVIEW.md), [validation](history/VALIDATION.md).
docs/IMPLEMENTATION_LOG.md:9054:The local reviewed research path now works from source and claims through thesis formation, evidence attachment, both product entrances and fixed-version tracking. The real database contains **27 sources, 161 claims, 19 theses, 64 current evaluations and 20 changes**. This phase added 114 reviewed claims from 18 additional extraction windows and 17 theses; all seven issuers are represented without a hardcoded ticker list. Usable extraction windows cover only 136,743 / 2,883,721 parsed characters (about 4.74%). This is partial processing coverage, not measured semantic recall.
docs/IMPLEMENTATION_LOG.md:9058:**M5:** implemented durable event/cursor persistence, targeted leases, frozen inference checkpoints, explicit review, crash recovery and idempotent admission/ACK. A real Microsoft evidence replay attached five assessments and one change to existing research. Replaying its model result, admission and event produced no new provider calls or research records. Jev authentication, typed labels and scoring now work. On 20 matched agent-authored evidence cases, Jev agreed with 19 labels and DeepSeek with 17; on 12 event cases, DeepSeek matched all categorical labels while Jev missed some relevance, novelty, modality and relation labels. These small synthetic comparisons are mixed evidence, not independent accuracy claims. Jev stays in shadow mode. The full current audit agreed on 62/64 assessments; both disagreements were reviewed against the originals and did not justify support.
docs/IMPLEMENTATION_LOG.md:9064:**Measured cost:** this continuation made **140 provider calls**, estimated **$0.247309506 off-peak / $0.491183118 peak**. Including earlier M3/M4, **180 calls total $0.326093514 / $0.648751134**. All completed calls occurred outside weekday peak windows, so the lower estimate applies to the observed schedule; neither value is a reconciled invoice. Failed, truncated, rejected and development calls are included. Independent Decimal arithmetic reconciled each archived response with the usage ledger; unresolved reservations are $0 and the unchanged continuation allocation is $8. Jev accounts for 30 calls / $0.003435894. TN/search data, coding-agent and review labor, storage/network and tax remain unmetered. [Raw-usage audit](../evals/history/usage-audits-2026-09-22-23/continued-2026-09-23-usage-audit.json), [final query chain costs](../evals/narrative-query-chain-cost-2026-09-23.json).
docs/IMPLEMENTATION_LOG.md:9066:**Milestone self-review and fixes:** exact-passage deduplication, auditing later evidence attachments, directed review jobs, timezone ordering, pending-poll state preservation, committed-intent checks before acknowledgement, bounded Jev rounding tolerance, question-constraint validation, cache invalidation, safe HTTP write modes and current CLI defaults were checked and corrected. Detailed findings and unresolved limits are in [CODE_REVIEW](history/CODE_REVIEW.md). Final verification: **237 tests**, both documented demos, 309 immutable context files, structural/provenance audit of all real research, and browser interaction checks passed. Final handoff checks are recorded in [VALIDATION](history/VALIDATION.md).
docs/IMPLEMENTATION_LOG.md:9076:Measured **22 calls**, including **12 synthetic prompt challenges and 10 real reconciliation/repeat calls**. Provider usage: **124,857 input / 73,259 output tokens**, including **50,598 reasoning tokens** in output. Dated peak/cache arithmetic independently recomputed: **$0.05252331–$0.10504662**, not a reconciled invoice. Synthetic experiments account for $0.021900228–$0.043800456; real attempts account for $0.030623082–$0.061246164. All failures are included; all calls reported usage and unresolved reservations are $0. Original $1 policy and 6,000 output-token limit were not increased. M3+M4 cumulative estimate: **$0.078784008–$0.157568016**. Jev calls: 0; no new TN calls; data billing, development and semantic-review effort remain unmetered. [Per-call audit](../evals/history/usage-audits-2026-09-22-23/m4-2026-09-23-usage-audit.json).
docs/IMPLEMENTATION_LOG.md:9078:Cost conclusion: API spend is small in this slice, but **22 calls for two reviewed hypotheses is not a production unit-cost estimate**. Twelve calls were rubric experiments; repeated truncation and semantic amendments are observable overhead. About 69% of output usage was reasoning. Tightening visible-answer prose did not reliably prevent truncation. Next work must measure recovery rate, untouched acceptance rate and review effort before extrapolating to a full universe or enabling Jev.
docs/IMPLEMENTATION_LOG.md:9106:Cost: **0 DeepSeek/Jev inference calls** in M2; no model-processing bill has been measured. TN/data-service billing is unknown and was not assumed free. Local CPU/storage and the coding assistant's own session cost are not metered by this repository. Archived responses and deterministic parser reuse avoid repeated downloads or cleaning; a complete 27-source admission replay added zero records.
docs/IMPLEMENTATION_LOG.md:9124:Measured **18 calls**: 3 smoke calls with prompt v1, 12 non-thinking v2 calls and 3 low-thinking v2 calls. Provider usage is **76,075 input / 30,927 output tokens**, including reasoning. Using observed cache usage and the dated official prices gives **$0.026260698 off-peak / $0.052521396 peak**. Calls occurred off-peak; these are schedule estimates, not reconciled invoices. All 18 calls have usage; unknown-billing reservations total $0. Jev calls: 0. TN billing and local/development/review costs remain unmetered. Budget policy: $1, reserving at peak before each request; no automatic increase. [Per-call audit](../evals/history/usage-audits-2026-09-22-23/m3-2026-09-22-usage-audit.json), [price source](https://api-docs.deepseek.com/quick_start/pricing/).
docs/IMPLEMENTATION_LOG.md:9145:User explicitly authorized the remaining local plan, replacing the earlier stop-before-M5 instruction. New paid-work caps total $8 across extraction, reconciliation, audits, Jev and narrative matching; allocations are in `config/models/continued-work-2026-09-23.json`. No remote, deployment or live trading added.
docs/IMPLEMENTATION_LOG.md:9151:First matched synthetic judge challenge: DeepSeek 17/20 and Jev 19/20 against frozen agent-authored labels. These are diagnostic counts, not independent quality calibration. Jev remains a shadow second-pass reviewer; no autonomous truth, trading, or admission authority.
