evals/bench-v1/gold/facts-test-a.json:1655:   "fact": "NVIDIA guided Q3 GAAP and non-GAAP gross margins to 74%, plus or minus 50 basis points.",
evals/bench-v1/gold/facts-test-a.json:1657:    "74%"
evals/bench-v1/gold/facts-test-a.json:1661:   "quote": "For Q3, we expect GAAP and non -GAAP gross margins to be 74%, plus or minus 50 basis points.",
evals/bench-v1/gold/queries.json:275:   "rationale": "NVIDIA risks: supply limits (about 70% growth versus roughly 100% demand), memory costs pushing gross margin guidance to 74% and a 71-72% Q4 trough, China excluded from the outlook after export controls, customer concentration (22% and 14% direct customers in FY2026), balance-sheet support and credit enhancement for AI labs that critics call circular financing, customers building their own chips, and scrutiny of AI spending. Microsoft (1): the Guardian's installed-chip investigation asks whether purchased NVIDIA chips are actually being deployed."
evals/bench-v1/gold/queries.json:291:   "rationale": "NVIDIA risks: supply limits (about 70% growth versus roughly 100% demand), memory costs pushing gross margin guidance to 74% and a 71-72% Q4 trough, China excluded from the outlook after export controls, customer concentration (22% and 14% direct customers in FY2026), balance-sheet support and credit enhancement for AI labs that critics call circular financing, customers building their own chips, and scrutiny of AI spending. Microsoft (1): the Guardian's installed-chip investigation asks whether purchased NVIDIA chips are actually being deployed."
evals/bench-v1/gold/queries.json:380:   "rationale": "Apple: memory costs drove the gross margin step-down (49.3% to 48.1% adjusted, guided to a 46.5% midpoint ex-refunds), called a '100-year flood'. NVIDIA: 'extreme pricing conditions in memory' reset gross margin guidance to 74% and a 71-72% Q4 trough. Amazon (1): its guidance risk factors cite supply volatility for memory chips. Tesla (1): it is building its own fab to secure 'essential logic and memory chips'."
