evals/refactor-2026-10/census/readmodel-cli.md:1:# Refactor census: `src/tn_hivemind/readmodel`, `src/tn_hivemind/cli`, `scripts/hivemind.py`\n\nScope read in full: 44 files, 13,286 lines (readmodel 8,829; cli 4,438; hivemind.py 19). Read-only; nothing edited, no tests run. Tools: `python3 -m pyflakes`, AST statistics, `git grep -w` for every top-level name across src/tests/evals/scripts/web, read-only SQLite counts on two local ledgers for the hot-path estimates.\n\n## Summary: the five mechanisms behind most findings\n\n1. **Versioned contracts built beside, not on, their predecessor.** Contract v1 (`contract_v1.py`, 889 lines, \"parked\" but still the default for belief ledgers via `web.contract_for` and `cli/dossier.py`) keeps private copies of helpers v2 later extracted (`_iso`≡`dates.iso_day`, `_week`≡`sections.week_start`, `_fye`≡`signals.fiscal_year_end`, `_statement_key`≡`data.claims.statement_key`, `_rel`/`_catalyst_parts` vs v2's), and `web.py`'s v1 payload functions re-inline validation that the v2 helpers (`_today`, `projection_entity`, `_snapshots`) already provide. The parked question stack (`answer`, `narrative`) and the feed each wrote their own `clip`. Produces most of the duplication findings.\n2. **The dossier row as one dict literal that gains a key per PRD item.** `build_row` (208 lines, ~90 keys), `stock_dossier` (193), `signal_views` (151), `company_timeline` (146), `entry_note` (104) are the product's unit rendered in one place; the per-row context (`fye_cache`, `calendar`, `snapshots`, `reports`, `replacement_notes`) is threaded positionally through four layers, giving the 7–12-parameter signatures. Produces the long-function and many-parameter findings.\n3. **Unindexed reads over a View whose `all(kind)` is a linear scan.** `loop.view.View.all` (loop/view.py:143–144) filters every head; the projection view indexes observations into the same `heads` dict, so a ledger that held 769 heads before the catalog stage holds 27,794 after it (asof-meta-run6c: 19,112 observations, 6,219 claims). `dossier.entity_card` scans `all('instrument')` per call and has 21 call sites, several inside per-driver/per-test loops; `records.resolve_entity` calls it per research entity per request; `fiscal_year_end_month(view.all('source'))` and `factors._records` re-read and re-filter whole record lists per surface. Produces the performance findings.\n4. **The daily orchestrator's library accreted in one module, with dependency injection by keyword, under an import order that forces inlined copies.** `daily.py` (1,150 lines, 64 functions, 11 banner sections; `preflight` 15 params, `health_report` 14) holds three variants of the \"-rN retry series\" idiom and one of four UTC-now formatters; `run.py` cannot import `daily` (documented order), so it inlined the `.sqlite3`-stem idiom three times. Produces the cli duplication and module-size findings.\n5. **Checklists written as one flat function per specification section.** `projection_checks.py` (851 lines; `identity_problems` 79, `shape_problems` 73, `run5_problems` 61), `guard_table` (120), `blocked_work` (108), `plan_recovery` (74), `common_flags`/`build_parser` (94/148) are lists of rules or flags that read fine as lists but exceed the length bound and, in `blocked_work`, open a SQLite connection inside nested loops.\n\nDead code is limited to four unused imports (pyflakes): `readmodel/view.py:20 cut_day` (genuinely unused) and `cli/daily.py:34 ledger_mark, ops_mark, usage_mark` (deliberate re-exports with `# noqa: F401` for `scripts/daily.py`). **No top-level function, class or constant in the reviewed modules is defined and never referenced** (every name reported by the scan as module-private has at least one real call line; single-use ones were checked against their call sites). The `COMMANDS` table and the three lock-mode sets in `app.py` are consistent (26 = 26).\n\n## Findings (JSON)\n\n```json\n[\n {\"id\":\"R01\",\"file\":\"src/tn_hivemind/readmodel/dossier.py:54\",\"category\":\"performance\",\"description\":\"entity_card scans every instrument head on each call, and View.all is itself a linear filter over all heads, so one call is O(heads).\",\"evidence\":\"loop/view.py:143-144 `all` = list comprehension over self.heads; 21 call sites in readmodel+cli (contract_v1 4, dossier 2, evidence 2, records 2, signals 2, web 2, answer/feed/narrative/questions/rows/sections/timeline 1 each); inside per-row (rows.py:298), per-test (signals.py:119 via next_check_of_test), per-print-driver (signals.py:239), per-development-role (evidence.py:87), per-linked-thesis (sections.py:95) loops; heads = 27,794 in .runtime/v4/asof-meta-run6c-2026-09-26.sqlite3 (769 before observations).\",\"estimate\":\"per stock dossier roughly rows x (1 + drivers x (tests + 1)) + developments x entity_roles calls, i.e. 10^2-10^3 calls x O(2.8e4) per render; per overview request once per research entity (634 entities in the asof ledger).\",\"mechanism\":\"a belief-era helper written when a View held hundreds of heads; the projection view later put 19k observations into the same heads dict (mechanism 3).\",\"refactor\":\"yes: memoize {issuer entity id: sorted symbols} once per view in view.memo (ProjectionView) or a view attribute (loop View), same output; the by-kind index belongs in loop.view (outside this scope).\"},\n {\"id\":\"R02\",\"file\":\"src/tn_hivemind/readmodel/records.py:19\",\"category\":\"performance\",\"description\":\"resolve_entity calls entity_card for every research entity on each name lookup, so a ticker lookup is O(entities x heads).\",\"evidence\":\"records.py:23-25; callers per request: web.py:360 (projection_entity), web.py:385, web.py:432; cli/dossier.py:20 per --entities name; questions.py:20 per ask.\",\"estimate\":\"once per dossier/timeline/stock route request and per CLI entity.\",\"mechanism\":\"same as R01.\",\"refactor\":\"yes: a symbol->entity map memoized per view; identical result (first match in research_entities order must be kept).\"},\n {\"id\":\"R03\",\"file\":\"src/tn_hivemind/readmodel/signals.py:293\",\"category\":\"long-function\",\"description\":\"signal_views is 151 lines with 12 parameters and five branches that each set a verdict dict and a next_check dict.\",\"evidence\":\"lines 293-443; branches at 357, 362, 372, 382, 384, 388; one test caller (tests) and rows.py:336.\",\"mechanism\":\"each PRD rule (not_reported, untestable, rescheduled, due/overdue, withdrawn tests, other companies' drivers) added a branch (mechanism 2).\",\"refactor\":\"yes: extract _driver_verdict (357-391), _driver_next_check (392-418) and _driver_out (420-437) and pass one row context object; dict key order kept so rendered documents are byte-identical.\"},\n {\"id\":\"R04\",\"file\":\"src/tn_hivemind/readmodel/signals.py:130\",\"category\":\"duplication\",\"description\":\"The same 8-key next_check dict (date, date_confidence, not_before, event_asset, overdue, window, candidates, label) is written as seven separate literals, and the provider-calendar-then-thesis-estimate block is duplicated.\",\"evidence\":\"dict literals at 130-133, 141-146, 235-237, 245-248, 249-250, 399-401, 403-405; confidence map {'estimated':..,'known':..,'confirmed':'known'} at 140 and 244; the report_event -> report_estimate -> confidence block at 135-146 and 238-248 differs only in `end` and `label`.\",\"mechanism\":\"driver_date (a bare driver) was copied from next_check_of_test (a test) (mechanism 1/2).\",\"refactor\":\"yes: one _next_check(**fields) constructor with the fixed key order and one _report_check(view, entity_id, end, today, calendar, snapshots, reports, label) helper; identical output as long as insertion order is preserved.\"},\n {\"id\":\"R05\",\"file\":\"src/tn_hivemind/readmodel/signals.py:192\",\"category\":\"duplication\",\"description\":\"fiscal_year_end is byte-identical to contract_v1._fye, both scanning view.all('source') on a cache miss and threading a plain-dict cache through four call layers.\",\"evidence\":\"signals.py:192-195 vs contract_v1.py:363-366; fye_cache passes company_timeline (timeline.py:142) -> build_row (rows.py:291) -> signal_views (signals.py:293) -> next_check_of_test (signals.py:110) and check_state calls at 341, 387, 391.\",\"mechanism\":\"v1's private copy kept beside v2's (mechanism 1); the cache is a parameter because no shared memo existed when written.\",\"refactor\":\"yes: one helper in records.py memoized in view.memo; dropping the fye_cache parameter changes four signatures (build_row has 1 test caller, signal_views 1), output unchanged.\"},\n {\"id\":\"R06\",\"file\":\"src/tn_hivemind/readmodel/rows.py:291\",\"category\":\"long-function\",\"description\":\"build_row is 208 lines with 8 parameters, returning one ~90-key literal, and evaluates row_coverage three times.\",\"evidence\":\"lines 291-498; row_coverage at rows.py:53 (in lineage_core), 316 and 439 (memoized in news_coverage.py:59, so repeat cost is a lookup).\",\"mechanism\":\"the row is the product's unit; every PRD field landed in the one literal (mechanism 2).\",\"refactor\":\"yes: bind the coverage once; extract _identity_block, _decision_block, _lifecycle_block, _evidence_block returning fragments merged in the same order; byte-identical.\"},\n {\"id\":\"R07\",\"file\":\"src/tn_hivemind/readmodel/timeline.py:282\",\"category\":\"long-function\",\"description\":\"stock_dossier is 193 lines (9 params) and company_timeline 146 lines; stock_dossier builds the 20-entry gaps prose and an 11-line rule string inline.\",\"evidence\":\"gaps at 330-373; rule prose at 432-442; summary block 405-422; company_timeline 134-279 with the upcoming-checks loop 178-192 and freshness block 196-206 inline.\",\"mechanism\":\"the reference contract's rule that every null needs an x_hivemind.gaps entry grew a gap per field (mechanism 2).\",\"refactor\":\"yes: hoist the rule prose to module constants (as BIAS_RULE and MARKS_RULE already are) and extract _gaps(...), _summary(...), _upcoming_checks(live); identical document.\"},\n {\"id\":\"R08\",\"file\":\"src/tn_hivemind/readmodel/timeline.py:297\",\"category\":\"duplication\",\"description\":\"The open-row predicate `lc not in ('resolved', 'invalidated')` is written six times and the open_rows list built at 297 is recomputed inline three times.\",\"evidence\":\"timeline.py:297, 302, 405, 455, 467; row_marks.py:120; projection_checks.py:79 holds RESOLVED but keeps its enums apart by design (its docstring).\",\"mechanism\":\"a literal copied per use; no home for the enum in reference.py (mechanism 2).\",\"refactor\":\"yes: a constant in reference.py and reuse of open_rows; identical.\"},\n {\"id\":\"R09\",\"file\":\"src/tn_hivemind/readmodel/timeline.py:155\",\"category\":\"readability\",\"description\":\"Five lambdas are bound to names, each carrying `# noqa: E731`.\",\"evidence\":\"timeline.py:155 order, sections.py:232 blank, news_coverage.py:77 count, cli/dossier.py:49 and :57 build.\",\"mechanism\":\"local style choice repeated.\",\"refactor\":\"yes: def statements; identical.\"},\n {\"id\":\"R10\",\"file\":\"src/tn_hivemind/readmodel/timeline.py:197\",\"category\":\"performance\",\"description\":\"The freshness block scans view.all('source') and evaluates published_date twice per source, then passes the list twice more, while news_coverage.source_payloads already memoizes the same payloads.\",\"evidence\":\"timeline.py:197-201; news_coverage.py:25-29.\",\"estimate\":\"once per dossier, O(sources) x 4 (373 sources in the asof ledger).\",\"mechanism\":\"three freshness fields added one at a time.\",\"refactor\":\"yes: compute (source, published) pairs once; identical.\"},\n {\"id\":\"R11\",\"file\":\"src/tn_hivemind/readmodel/feed.py:147\",\"category\":\"duplication\",\"description\":\"clip is defined three times with byte-identical bodies.\",\"evidence\":\"feed.py:147-149, answer.py:216-218, narrative.py:56-58.\",\"mechanism\":\"the parked question stack and the feed were written apart (mechanism 1).\",\"refactor\":\"yes: one clip (records.py or a text helper) imported by the three; identical.\"},\n {\"id\":\"R12\",\"file\":\"src/tn_hivemind/readmodel/contract_v1.py:1\",\"category\":\"module-too-large\",\"description\":\"The parked v1 contract (889 lines, three functions over 60 lines) keeps private copies of helpers that v2 later extracted, and is still live for belief ledgers.\",\"evidence\":\"_iso (130) == dates.iso_day; _week (725) == sections.week_start; _fye (363) == signals.fiscal_year_end; _statement_key (457) == data.claims.statement_key (identical body); _date (119) == core.periods.day except that a datetime is returned as itself rather than .date(); _rel (776) vs snapshots.holder_rows; _catalyst_parts (763) vs signals.catalyst_parts; LABELS_ZH (104) vs i18n. Live callers: web.py:382, 429 (default on ledgers without development heads), cli/dossier.py:42, 94; tests test_readmodel_contract_v1.py, test_readmodel_timeline.py, test_loop_reconcile_profile.py:246-330.\",\"mechanism\":\"v2 was built beside v1 and v1 parked rather than retired (mechanism 1; retention S25 keeps it until adopted).\",\"refactor\":\"partly: sharing _iso, _week, _fye, _statement_key is behaviour-preserving (identical bodies); deleting the module or merging _rel/_catalyst_parts changes v1 output and is a DECISIONS/retention matter, not a refactor.\"},\n {\"id\":\"R13\",\"file\":\"src/tn_hivemind/readmodel/web.py:379\",\"category\":\"duplication\",\"description\":\"The v1 payload functions re-inline validation that the v2 helpers provide: the today regex, the lang check, the entity-resolve-or-404 and the snapshot loads.\",\"evidence\":\"_today at 343 vs inline regex at 388-390 and 435-437; lang check 402-404 and 438-440; resolve_entity + 404 at 360-362 (projection_entity), 385-387, 432-434; load_snapshot(server.calendar_path/holders_path) at 392-393 and 441-442 vs _snapshots at 350-354.\",\"mechanism\":\"v2 routes added beside v1; v1 not rebased on the new helpers (mechanism 1).\",\"refactor\":\"yes: route v1 through _today, a _lang helper and a belief-view resolver with the same 400/404 strings; responses identical.\"},\n {\"id\":\"R14\",\"file\":\"src/tn_hivemind/readmodel/web.py:830\",\"category\":\"long-function\",\"description\":\"make_server takes 15 parameters, six of them runtime file paths and three model-client inputs.\",\"evidence\":\"lines 830-833; 7 files under tests/evals call make_server or serve; cli/dossier.py:115 passes 11 of them.\",\"mechanism\":\"each runtime file became a keyword; cli.runtime.RuntimePaths cannot be imported (layering: cli sits above readmodel).\",\"refactor\":\"yes: a readmodel-local frozen dataclass of server files passed as one argument, with the old keywords kept as a shim so the 7 callers and the layering are untouched.\"},\n {\"id\":\"R15\",\"file\":\"src/tn_hivemind/readmodel/web.py:322\",\"category\":\"readability\",\"description\":\"Server attributes are read inconsistently: getattr-with-default in the v2 helpers, direct attribute access in the v1 payloads, and projection_views is created lazily although make_server assigns it None.\",\"evidence\":\"getattr at 322, 352-354, 412; direct access at 392-393, 441-442, 445; server.projection_views = None at 864.\",\"mechanism\":\"attributes bolted onto ThreadingHTTPServer in make_server; getattr defaults let tests build bare servers.\",\"refactor\":\"yes: set every attribute in make_server and read them directly; identical behaviour for servers built by make_server (tests constructing bare servers would need the attributes).\"},\n {\"id\":\"R16\",\"file\":\"src/tn_hivemind/readmodel/web.py:155\",\"category\":\"performance\",\"description\":\"ViewCache.get holds the cache lock across a whole View build (a full ledger read), so every request on every as_of waits behind a cold build; db_signature stats two files per request.\",\"evidence\":\"web.py:167-183 (lock acquired at 170, store read 175-179 inside it); db_signature 134-143 called at 168 and in SearchService.open 567.\",\"estimate\":\"one ledger read per (db change, as_of); two stat calls per request.\",\"mechanism\":\"a design choice for read-only consistency.\",\"refactor\":\"no change proposed (a per-key build lock would alter concurrency semantics the tests may rely on); noted only.\"},\n {\"id\":\"R17\",\"file\":\"src/tn_hivemind/readmodel/evidence.py:178\",\"category\":\"performance\",\"description\":\"evidence_list rebuilds claim_judgments by iterating every evaluation of every view of the row for every evidence item.\",\"evidence\":\"lines 214-224 nested in the per-item loop starting 189; sorted at 225 by ids.\",\"estimate\":\"O(items x views x evaluations) per row, once per dossier render (asof ledger: 391 developments, 167 dispositions).\",\"mechanism\":\"a history-only field added inside the item loop.\",\"refactor\":\"yes: build {claim id: [evaluation]} per lineage once before the loop; identical (sort key is ids).\"},\n {\"id\":\"R18\",\"file\":\"src/tn_hivemind/readmodel/sections.py:71\",\"category\":\"performance\",\"description\":\"linked_drivers walks every thesis row of every company and, per row, every development of this company; thesis_rows(view) re-sorts its index per call and is called four times per dossier.\",\"evidence\":\"sections.py:77-87; drivers.thesis_rows (loop/drivers.py:832-834) sorts rows on each call; callers rows.py:37, sections.py:77, ranking.py:73, ranking.py:100.\",\"estimate\":\"O(rows_all x devs_mine) + 4 sorts per dossier.\",\"mechanism\":\"the cross-company section reads the whole row index instead of an inverted decisions index.\",\"refactor\":\"yes: invert row_index(view).decisions once by development; identical list.\"},\n {\"id\":\"R19\",\"file\":\"src/tn_hivemind/readmodel/sections.py:163\",\"category\":\"performance\",\"description\":\"claim_rows, for a development without own decisions, scans every deciding entity, and resolves source_of(claim_of(...)) per restating member per fact.\",\"evidence\":\"lines 171-173 and 197-198.\",\"estimate\":\"once per dossier; O(devs x deciders) + O(facts x restatements).\",\"mechanism\":\"the cross-company fallback was appended as a nested comprehension.\",\"refactor\":\"yes: precompute decided_by_entity inverted by development; identical.\"},\n {\"id\":\"R20\",\"file\":\"src/tn_hivemind/readmodel/ranking.py:166\",\"category\":\"performance\",\"description\":\"row_bearing is computed twice per unranked company row, and row_headline_key (which calls news_developments -> drivers.evidence_moves and drivers.context_items, neither memoized) is evaluated up to four times per live row.\",\"evidence\":\"row_bearing at 179 (median) and 190 (role); row_headline_key in choose_headline at 259, 272, 280, 281 and timeline.py:162 (most_active); evidence_moves/context_items (loop/drivers.py:1330, 1511) walk deciders x decided developments x decision rows each call.\",\"estimate\":\"per dossier about 2 x rows row_bearing and up to 4 x live rows x (evidence_moves + context_items).\",\"mechanism\":\"the headline rule gained tiers (rank, debate rank, exposure role, role, fallback) each re-scoring.\",\"refactor\":\"yes: compute row_bearing once into the row context and memoize news_developments per (row id, today) in view.memo; identical order.\"},\n {\"id\":\"R21\",\"file\":\"src/tn_hivemind/readmodel/closes.py:124\",\"category\":\"performance\",\"description\":\"prediction_states is recomputed for each open view in settled_tests and again in signal_views for the current view; it is not memoized.\",\"evidence\":\"closes.py:133 and signals.py:309; loop/predictions.py:683-730 has no memo.\",\"estimate\":\"2 x per row with one open view; per dossier.\",\"mechanism\":\"two readers of the same reader result written apart.\",\"refactor\":\"yes: memo per (thesis id, version, today) in view.memo; identical.\"},\n {\"id\":\"R22\",\"file\":\"src/tn_hivemind/readmodel/projection_checks.py:1\",\"category\":\"module-too-large\",\"description\":\"The checker is 851 lines with three functions over 60 lines; it is test and eval support only (no production import).\",\"evidence\":\"identity_problems 267-345 (79), shape_problems 150-222 (73), run5_problems 692-752 (61); _keys 7 params; docstring says no production module imports it.\",\"mechanism\":\"one check appended per PRD section item (mechanism 5).\",\"refactor\":\"yes: split into shape, identity, state and marks modules re-exported from projection_checks; identical problem strings, so evals/projection-v2/acceptance.py and tests see no change.\"},\n {\"id\":\"R23\",\"file\":\"src/tn_hivemind/readmodel/factors.py:23\",\"category\":\"performance\",\"description\":\"Every factor surface re-opens the research store and the ops sidecar, re-sorts all records, and re-filters the full record list per factor and per column.\",\"evidence\":\"_records 23-41 opens ResearchStore at 30 and sorts at 41, called by world (237), factor_lane (350), stock (391), flows_page_json (403); _loop_dates 76-90 opens the sidecar at 84 per call; world calls _partition(records, column) per column (246) and _factor_data per factor per column (249); flows_page_json calls _lane per factor (414) and _stock per instrument (435), and _factor_data (177-205) filters ladders, band_changes, assessments, factors and the whole record list for prints on every call.\",\"estimate\":\"per flows page: O(factors x records) + O(instruments x loadings x records); per world: O(columns x factors x records).\",\"mechanism\":\"pure functions over a flat record list with no index (mechanism 3).\",\"refactor\":\"yes: index _partition output by factor id and kind once and pass it down; outputs are deep-copied already, so identical.\"},\n {\"id\":\"R24\",\"file\":\"src/tn_hivemind/readmodel/view.py:20\",\"category\":\"dead-code\",\"description\":\"cut_day is imported and never used.\",\"evidence\":\"pyflakes: '.dates.cut_day' imported but unused; no other reference in the module.\",\"mechanism\":\"left behind by a refactor of the cut logic into ProjectionView.day_cut.\",\"refactor\":\"yes: delete the import.\"},\n {\"id\":\"R25\",\"file\":\"src/tn_hivemind/readmodel/records.py:89\",\"category\":\"readability\",\"description\":\"repeat_signal performs two function-local imports on a path called per development member.\",\"evidence\":\"lines 108 and 112; callers evidence.py:36, 70 and sections.py:158 inside member loops; data sits below readmodel so no cycle forces the lazy import.\",\"mechanism\":\"a lazy import kept after the cycle it avoided went away.\",\"refactor\":\"yes: hoist to module imports; identical.\"},\n {\"id\":\"R26\",\"file\":\"src/tn_hivemind/readmodel/snapshots.py:18\",\"category\":\"error-handling\",\"description\":\"Three loaders read the same provider snapshot files: snapshots.load_snapshot and i18n.load_cache raise on malformed JSON (a 500 from web._api, a traceback from cmd_timeline) while cli/options.read_snapshot wraps the same read in a SystemExit message.\",\"evidence\":\"snapshots.py:18-26, i18n.py:38-42, cli/options.py:173-180.\",\"mechanism\":\"each consumer wrote its own loader (mechanism 1).\",\"refactor\":\"partly: one loader can serve all three only if the CLI keeps its SystemExit wrapper; readmodel's raising behaviour must stay (tests for the 500 path).\"},\n {\"id\":\"R27\",\"file\":\"src/tn_hivemind/readmodel/rows.py:156\",\"category\":\"readability\",\"description\":\"About 100 lines (argued_reason_whole, lineage_reasons, question_asked, whole_text, whole_strings, full_stance_history) un-clip in the reader what the debates writer clipped.\",\"evidence\":\"rows.py:156-262 and 483-494; docstrings cite debates.rows.clip and debates.exposure.exposure_debate as the clipping writers.\",\"mechanism\":\"a reader compensating for a writer (AGENTS lesson 33: fix the writer); kept because stored records already carry the clipped text.\",\"refactor\":\"no behaviour-preserving removal: stored records keep the clipped strings; only a writer change (outside this scope) would retir