evals/refactor-2026-10/census/core-models.md:1:REFACTOR CENSUS: src/tn_hivemind/core and src/tn_hivemind/models (21 files, 6,374 lines, 369 functions). Read-only; nothing edited, no tests run. Evidence sources: full read of every file; an AST census; a word-boundary reference scan of every defined name over src/tests/evals/scripts (741 files); pyflakes (one finding: ledger.py:28 `ClockNotSet` imported but unused, a `# noqa: F401` re-export); row counts and EXPLAIN QUERY PLAN on two real ledgers (.runtime/v4/stage2-accept-v142-2026-10-12: 17,012 records, 869 transactions over 2 loop days = 434 bundles/day, avg 19.6 records per bundle, max 400; sources avg 6 KB, max 527 KB; .runtime/v4/golden-v2-2026-09-30: 21,704 records, pre-order ledger without tx/seq) and on the usage ledger (.runtime/pipeline/usage.sqlite3: 77,699 calls, 564 budgets, 557 with an aggregate cap). Per-pass figures below are estimates from those counts, not timings.\n\nTwo constraints every refactor here must carry, stated up front: (1) `usage.request_key` hashes `json_bytes(request)`, the context and the policy dict, so any change to request construction order or policy dicts re-keys the cache; (2) `rule_registry.describe` hashes a function's *source text*, so a stored `rule_definition` sha256 changes when any function a registered rule declares (in loop/data, outside these packages) is reformatted; refactors inside rule_registry itself do not change digests as long as `canonical` keeps producing identical bytes.\n\nSUMMARY: the five mechanisms behind most findings\n1. Copy-and-extend instead of calling the base. The models package (transport -> providers -> embeddings -> llm/jev) holds five copies of the credential-shape check, two of the timeout/deadline block, a second `run_model` (Embedder._dispatch) and a second `LLM.__init__` (Embedder.__init__); core holds the publication-precision rule twice (contracts/manifest, identical messages), the exact-substring scan three times (documents), and canonical-JSON+sha256 three times (archive, rule_registry, ledger.short_hash).\n2. Invariants accreted inline at the write path. `append_bundle` (clock S37, order S69, lock S201) and `validate_record` (12 kinds in one elif chain) grew by appending; `Ledger.admit` pre-screens what the store re-checks, so each record is canonical-dumped 3x and fetched 2x before insert, and `validate_dependencies` fetches and JSON-decodes every dependency twice (generic loop, then the per-kind loop) — for claims that is the whole source document.\n3. SQL whose access pattern the primary key does not serve, run per bundle or per reservation: `MAX(tx), MAX(seq)` full scan on every append_bundle; the cache sync walking every index entry of a kind per commit; `Embedder.cached` reading every vector of the model per develop pass; the aggregate-cap check scanning the whole `calls` table in Python per fresh reservation.\n4. Core holding upper-layer shapes by name: `_thesis_dependencies` (six loop-owned kinds), `_legacy_passes` (loop's `run_inputs` table), `CachingStore.view_reuse/shared_view` (loop.view), the extraction window tables inside `Ledger`, and `history_positions` (a test fixture helper). Registration exists for rules (RULE_OWNERS) but not for these.\n5. Modules written apart from the house style and never reconciled: jev.py (compressed, 26 no-space-after-comma lines), rules.py (double quotes only), rule_registry.py (import-free, own canonical/digest), three annotated signatures in store.py, two different `IDENTITY_KINDS`, two `PARSER_VERSION`s, a transport docstring claiming `jev.Jev` subclasses `ProviderTransport` when it does not.\n\nFINDINGS (JSON)\n[\n{\"id\":\"D1\",\"file\":\"src/tn_hivemind/core/units.py:26\",\"category\":\"dead-code\",\"description\":\"MONEY_UNITS is defined and referenced nowhere.\",\"evidence\":\"grep -rnw MONEY_UNITS over src, tests, evals, scripts, docs, config: only the definition; siblings ADDITIVE_UNITS/UNIT_CLASS have 10 production refs (data/observations.py 6, loop/comparisons.py 2, loop/due.py 2).\",\"mechanism\":\"accretion: added with its siblings, never consumed.\",\"refactor\":\"delete; no behaviour change.\"},\n{\"id\":\"D2\",\"file\":\"src/tn_hivemind/core/store.py:644\",\"category\":\"dead-code\",\"description\":\"ResearchStore.list_records is reached only from tests while Ledger.heads (ledger.py:271-278) re-implements its latest-per-id fold.\",\"evidence\":\"references: tests/test_core_store.py 6, tests/test_data_intake.py 5, tests/test_core_manifest.py 3, tests/test_core_clock.py 1; zero in src outside its definition; ledger.py:274-278 is the same fold over record_snapshot([kind]).\",\"mechanism\":\"the ledger grew its own reader beside the store's.\",\"refactor\":\"Ledger.heads non-cached branch -> self.store.list_records(kind): snapshot is ORDER BY kind, record_id, version, so first-seen id order equals sorted id order; identical list.\"},\n{\"id\":\"D3\",\"file\":\"src/tn_hivemind/core/store.py:265\",\"category\":\"dead-code\",\"description\":\"ResearchStore.history_positions has no production caller; it exists for the stored-history test fixtures.\",\"evidence\":\"references: tests/stored_history.py 2, tests/readmodel_timeline_support.py 1, tests/test_knowledge_order.py 1 (a registry entry); none in src.\",\"mechanism\":\"test-fixture support placed in core (also a layering fact, Y6).\",\"refactor\":\"move into tests/stored_history.py, which already wraps it; no production path changes.\"},\n{\"id\":\"D4\",\"file\":\"src/tn_hivemind/models/usage.py:453\",\"category\":\"dead-code\",\"description\":\"UsageLedgerReader.spent_under is test-only; production reaches _spent_nano_under through reserve.\",\"evidence\":\"one reference: tests/test_models_transport_usage.py:254.\",\"mechanism\":\"a reader mirror added for symmetry with spent().\",\"refactor\":\"keep or delete; no behaviour change.\"},\n{\"id\":\"D5\",\"file\":\"src/tn_hivemind/core/ledger.py:172,280\",\"category\":\"dead-code\",\"description\":\"CachingStore.verify_cache / Ledger.verify_read_cache are test-only by design (documented as a test and replay-harness check).\",\"evidence\":\"one reference: tests/test_loop_reconcile_dates.py:73.\",\"mechanism\":\"a deliberate check hook.\",\"refactor\":\"none needed; listed as a fact.\"},\n{\"id\":\"D6\",\"file\":\"src/tn_hivemind/core/documents.py:277\",\"category\":\"dead-code\",\"description\":\"sections(text, document_type='') never reads document_type; windows() (417) threads it only to pass it here; context_card (451) uses it only as an output field.\",\"evidence\":\"body lines 282-301 contain no use of document_type; evals/n9-phase1-risk/acceptance1.py:72 passes document_type= to windows.\",\"mechanism\":\"a parameter reserved for a per-document-type split that never came.\",\"refactor\":\"keeping the kwarg accepted and ignored is byte-identical; removing it only changes call signatures.\"},\n{\"id\":\"D7\",\"file\":\"src/tn_hivemind/models/transport.py:233,245\",\"category\":\"dead-code\",\"description\":\"_WatchedHTTPConnection (plain HTTP) is registered but unreachable: every endpoint in the package is https.\",\"evidence\":\"providers.py:12, embeddings.py:52, jev.py:10, truenorth.py:13 all https; _WATCHED_CONNECTIONS maps both urllib classes.\",\"mechanism\":\"symmetry with urllib's HTTP/HTTPS handler pair.\",\"refactor\":\"removable with no observable change; harmless to keep.\"},\n{\"id\":\"D8\",\"file\":\"src/tn_hivemind/core/ledger.py:28\",\"category\":\"dead-code\",\"description\":\"ClockNotSet imported and re-exported with noqa, unused in the module (the only pyflakes finding in both packages).\",\"evidence\":\"pyflakes: \\\"'.store.ClockNotSet' imported but unused\\\"; ClockNotSet has 4 refs in src outside core.\",\"mechanism\":\"re-export for callers that import it from ledger.\",\"refactor\":\"none; fact.\"},\n{\"id\":\"U1\",\"file\":\"src/tn_hivemind/models/transport.py:284; providers.py:59; embeddings.py:113; jev.py:16; truenorth.py:47\",\"category\":\"duplication\",\"description\":\"The credential-shape check `not isinstance(key, str) or not key or any(ch.isspace() for ch in key)` is written five times; StructuredOpenAI and EmbeddingClient subclass ProviderTransport but never call its __init__, which holds the first copy.\",\"evidence\":\"grep 'any(c.isspace() for c in|any(ch.isspace() for ch in' in models: 5 hits; base message is provider_name + ' key is missing or malformed' = 'OpenAI key is missing or malformed', the literal both OpenAI clients raise.\",\"mechanism\":\"each client copied the transport's constructor instead of calling it.\",\"refactor\":\"both OpenAI clients call ProviderTransport.__init__ (message text identical via provider_name); jev/truenorth keep theirs (different exception classes).\"},\n{\"id\":\"U2\",\"file\":\"src/tn_hivemind/models/providers.py:61-72 vs embeddings.py:82-84,116-124\",\"category\":\"duplication\",\"description\":\"timeout_seconds bound (same message 'policy timeout_seconds must be within (0, 900]'), the field assignments and the `deadline` property are copied between StructuredOpenAI and EmbeddingClient.\",\"evidence\":\"grep 'timeout_seconds must be within': providers.py:63, embeddings.py:84; grep 'return self._deadline if is_watched': providers.py:72, embeddings.py:124.\",\"mechanism\":\"EmbeddingClient copied from StructuredOpenAI.\",\"refactor\":\"move the bound check and the property into ProviderTransport; same values, same messages.\"},\n{\"id\":\"U3\",\"file\":\"src/tn_hivemind/models/embeddings.py:494-511 (_dispatch), 464-492 (_run)\",\"category\":\"duplication\",\"description\":\"Embedder._dispatch repeats usage.run_model's send/archive/finish body (usage.py:595-614) line for line; Embedder._run repeats LLM.call's reserve-then-retry shape (llm.py:99-117).\",\"evidence\":\"same failure strings in both ('invalid_response_envelope', 'invalid_response_json', str(exc)); _dispatch computes unbilled from UNBILLED_HTTP without run_model's transport check because EmbeddingUsageLedger.unbilled_transports covers it.\",\"mechanism\":\"run_model validates the structured transport at usage.py:583-586, so embeddings re-implemented it rather than branching.\",\"refactor\":\"an embeddings branch in run_model (validate_request) lets _run call run_model; ledger rows and archive objects are built from the same fields and strings, so stored calls stay identical.\"},\n{\"id\":\"U4\",\"file\":\"src/tn_hivemind/models/llm.py:60-83 vs embeddings.py:313-351\",\"category\":\"duplication\",\"description\":\"LLM.__init__ and Embedder.__init__ share archive coercion, ledger_path mkdir, the budget_conflict check (same BUDGET_IMMUTABLE message), the client-vs-deadline exclusivity check (same message), _local/_lock/calls; LLM._ledger and Embedder.usage are the same per-thread ledger getter.\",\"evidence\":\"lines cited; messages identical.\",\"mechanism\":\"copy.\",\"refactor\":\"a shared base for budgeted clients; construction only, no request bytes involved.\"},\n{\"id\":\"U5\",\"file\":\"src/tn_hivemind/core/rule_registry.py:25-32; ledger.py:33\",\"category\":\"duplication\",\"description\":\"rule_registry.canonical/digest re-implement archive.json_bytes/sha256 with identical json.dumps arguments; ledger.short_hash is a third sha256(json_bytes()).\",\"evidence\":\"json.dumps(value, sort_keys=True, separators=(',', ':'), ensure_ascii=False, allow_nan=False).encode('utf-8') appears at archive.py:36-37 and rule_registry.py:27-28.\",\"mechanism\":\"rule_registry was written import-free.\",\"refactor\":\"`from .archive import json_bytes as canonical` yields identical bytes, hence identical rule digests (verifiable by re-hashing a stored rule_definition).\"},\n{\"id\":\"U6\",\"file\":\"src/tn_hivemind/core/documents.py:151-154,184-192,217-220; 60-68 vs 82-88\",\"category\":\"duplication\",\"description\":\"Three copies of the exact-substring scan loop (locate_all, locate_quote's windowed branch, locate); locate is locate_all + nearest-to-hint differing only by ignore_case; CompactText.fold repeats __init__'s folding loop minus positions/footers.\",\"evidence\":\"grep 'text.find(quote' in documents.py: lines 151,154,186,217,220.\",\"mechanism\":\"each quote-location profile added a copy rather than a parameter (docstring 162-168: 'Legacy profiles').\",\"refactor\":\"one _exact_spans(text, quote, limit, accept) generator; result order and limits unchanged.\"},\n{\"id\":\"U7\",\"file\":\"src/tn_hivemind/core/ledger.py:299-308; store.py:482,516-521; store.py:395-404\",\"category\":\"duplication\",\"description\":\"Three layers defend the immutability invariant: Ledger.admit pre-screens (store.get + normalize_record), append_bundle normalises and fetches again and compares canonical JSON twice (520), _insert_record serialises and checks existence a third time (same message 'existing record version is immutable' at 403 and 521).\",\"evidence\":\"grep normalize_record|canonical_payload_json in ledger.py/store.py: 305, 395, 482, 520(x2).\",\"mechanism\":\"each layer written to stand alone.\",\"refactor\":\"admit may hand its normalised records to the store; the pre-screen's early `return 0` (no clock needed) and the StaleHeadError-before-ValueError precedence must be kept.\"},\n{\"id\":\"U8\",\"file\":\"src/tn_hivemind/core/contracts.py:342-351 vs manifest.py:36-53\",\"category\":\"duplication\",\"description\":\"The publication-precision rule (timestamp/date/unknown) is duplicated with identical message strings.\",\"evidence\":\"'date-only publication requires YYYY-MM-DD' at contracts.py:348 and manifest.py:45; 'unknown publication time must be null' at contracts.py:351 and manifest.py:42.\",\"mechanism\":\"copied from contracts into manifest.\",\"refactor\":\"one helper in contracts; manifest adds its not-after-created_at check afterwards; messages identical.\"},\n{\"id\":\"U9\",\"file\":\"src/tn_hivemind/core/store.py:187-191 vs 198-201\",\"category\":\"duplication\",\"description\":\"ResearchStore.__init__ repeats the PRAGMA column read that _reread_columns performs.\",\"evidence\":\"lines cited.\",\"mechanism\":\"_reread_columns added later for the rollback path.\",\"refactor\":\"__init__ calls _reread_columns(); identical.\"},\n{\"id\":\"U10\",\"file\":\"src/tn_hivemind/core/store.py:422,452; models/usage.py:141,479\",\"category\":\"duplication\",\"description\":\"The write_lock table-existence query appears twice; the call_recoveries existence query appears twice with two WHERE forms (name= vs type='table' AND name=).\",\"evidence\":\"grep sqlite_master in core/models: 5 hits.\",\"mechanism\":\"ad hoc.\",\"refactor\":\"a _table_exists helper; same answers.\"},\n{\"id\":\"U11\",\"file\":\"src/tn_hivemind/core/table_evidence.py:17-19 vs periods.py:17-18\",\"category\":\"duplication\",\"description\":\"Two month-name tables; table_evidence's also builds its _MONTH regex from its keys.\",\"evidence\":\"lines cited; periods.MONTHS includes abbreviations.\",\"mechanism\":\"modules written apart.\",\"refactor\":\"not behaviour-preserving without filtering (the regex would gain abbreviations); listed, not recommended.\"},\n{\"id\":\"U12\",\"file\":\"src/tn_hivemind/models/truenorth.py:38-41 vs transport.py:40-43\",\"category\":\"duplication\",\"description\":\"_NoRedirect and NoRedirect are the same handler raising different exception classes (MCPError vs ModelError).\",\"evidence\":\"lines cited.\",\"mechanism\":\"truenorth kept its own error type.\",\"refactor\":\"not mergeable without changing the raised type; fact.\"},\n{\"id\":\"U13\",\"file\":\"src/tn_hivemind/models/jev.py:44-54\",\"category\":\"duplication\",\"description\":\"Jev.complete re-implements ProviderTransport._post (request build, bounded read, key-echo refusal, HTTPError mapping).\",\"evidence\":\"compare jev.py:44-54 with transport.py:294-318; jev.py:13 `class Jev:` does not subclass.\",\"mechanism\":\"Jev predates the transport base.\",\"refactor\":\"subclassing would change stored failure strings ('Jev HTTP 401' -> 'model HTTP 401'), so it is not byte-identical for jev calls; only the docstring correction (R8) is free.\"},\n{\"id\":\"U14\",\"file\":\"src/tn_hivemind/core/ledger.py:90-94,271-278; store.py:647-650\",\"category\":\"duplication\",\"description\":\"Three latest-version-per-id folds (_Kind.heads, Ledger.heads, ResearchStore.list_records).\",\"evidence\":\"lines cited.\",\"mechanism\":\"see D2.\",\"refactor\":\"see D2.\"},\n{\"id\":\"U15\",\"file\":\"src/tn_hivemind/core/periods.py:144-149 vs 39-49\",\"category\":\"duplication\",\"description\":\"published_date(source) equals day(source['payload'].get('published_at')) (same str()[:10] + fromisoformat + None on ValueError).\",\"evidence\":\"published_date has 19 production refs; day is imported in 10 modules (4 as as_date).\",\"mechanism\":\"a convenience alias.\",\"refactor\":\"define published_date as that one-liner; identical.\"},\n{\"id\":\"L1\",\"file\":\"src/tn_hivemind/core/contracts.py:280\",\"category\":\"long-function\",\"description\":\"validate_record is 200 lines: one if/elif chain over 12 kinds plus a shared tail.\",\"evidence\":\"AST: 280-479; branches at 300, 323, 328, 352, 364, 418, 421, 431, 440, 470.\",\"mechanism\":\"every core kind's rules were appended in place while higher-layer kinds got registration (docstring 16-23).\",\"refactor\":\"per-kind functions dispatched by a dict, statement order inside each branch preserved so the first-raised message is unchanged.\"},\n{\"id\":\"L2\",\"file\":\"src/tn_hivemind/core/store.py:460\",\"category\":\"long-function\",\"description\":\"append_bundle is 124 lines: guard parsing, lock, existence, clock stamp, order numbering, version monotonicity, head guards, consecutive versions, lookup, cycle check, dependency validation, insert, transaction row.\",\"evidence\":\"AST: 460-583.\",\"mechanism\":\"the clock (S37), the order (S69) and the lock (S201) were added inline.\",\"refactor\":\"extract _parse_guards / _stamp_and_number / _check_heads; keep the exception order.\"},\n{\"id\":\"L3\",\"file\":\"src/tn_hivemind/core/table_evidence.py:192\",\"category\":\"long-function\",\"description\":\"_parse is 111 lines carrying a 5-tuple row candidate unpacked three times.\",\"evidence\":\"tuple built at 236, unpacked at 254, 258, 266 with `_` placeholders.\",\"mechanism\":\"single-pass parser grown in place.\",\"refactor\":\"a named row-candidate record and a _parse_rows helper; output JSON unchanged.\"},\n{\"id\":\"L4\",\"file\":\"src/tn_hivemind/core/manifest.py:56\",\"category\":\"long-function\",\"description\":\"validate_manifest is 118 lines; the per-document loop (99-145) is 47 lines of field checks.\",\"evidence\":\"AST.\",\"mechanism\":\"one validator function.\",\"refactor\":\"_validate_document(doc, resolve, members); same messages, same order.\"},\n{\"id\":\"L5\",\"file\":\"src/tn_hivemind/core/rule_registry.py:166,254,298\",\"category\":\"long-function\",\"description\":\"executable_references is 86 lines with three nested closures; describe 42; build_definition has 10 parameters and a nested visit.\",\"evidence\":\"AST.\",\"mechanism\":\"content-addressing had to enumerate every reference source.\",\"refactor\":\"possible inside the module without changing digests as long as canonical/normalized/describe output stays identical; note the source-hash constraint for rule functions outside this package.\"},\n{\"id\":\"L6\",\"file\":\"src/tn_hivemind/models/usage.py:217; core/archive.py:192; core/parsing.py:134\",\"category\":\"long-function\",\"description\":\"reserve 70 lines (retry-token path, budget check, aggregate-cap loop, insert); fetch_public 62 (redirect loop + bounded read); parse_bytes 61 (html, pdf, text in one function).\",\"evidence\":\"AST.\",\"mechanism\":\"accretion.\",\"refactor\":\"parse_bytes splits cleanly by format; reserve's aggregate-cap block is a natural helper (see P5).\"},\n{\"id\":\"M1\",\"file\":\"src/tn_hivemind/core/documents.py\",\"category\":\"module-too-large\",\"description\":\"480 lines holding four concerns the docstring itself lists: quote location (14-228), sections (231-324), windows/render/blank (327-438), context cards (441-480).\",\"evidence\":\"section markers at 231 and 441; 26 functions.\",\"mechanism\":\"'document preparation' as one bucket.\",\"refactor\":\"split into quotes/sections/windows modules with core.documents re-exporting names (data/claims.py, data/relations.py:32 import from it).\"},\n{\"id\":\"M2\",\"file\":\"src/tn_hivemind/core/ledger.py\",\"category\":\"module-too-large\",\"description\":\"523 lines: CachingStore (65-187), clock+admit (190-363), bootstrap (365-387), entity/source views (390-414), extraction window bookkeeping (417-482), ReadOnlyLedger, _thesis_dependencies.\",\"evidence\":\"44 functions; window methods have their callers in data/ (record_window 6 refs, window_resolved 4).\",\"mechanism\":\"the ops sidecar's tables were created where the connection lives.\",\"refactor\":\"window bookkeeping into its own module over ledger.ops; same SQL.\"},\n{\"id\":\"M3\",\"file\":\"src/tn_hivemind/models/embeddings.py\",\"category\":\"module-too-large\",\"description\":\"531 lines: client+usage glue (64-174), canonical store incl. the seed_store tool (177-299), Embedder (302-519), numpy matrix (522-531).\",\"evidence\":\"33 functions; seed_store is reached from scripts/embed_store.py.\",\"mechanism\":\"the store was added beside the embedder (docstring 27-30).\",\"refactor\":\"EmbeddingStore+seed_store into embed_store.py; imports only.\"},\n{\"id\":\"M4\",\"file\":\"src/tn_hivemind/models/usage.py\",\"category\":\"module-too-large\",\"description\":\"614 lines: ledger writer (157-379), reader (396-502), retry policy (533-572), run_model (575-614).\",\"evidence\":\"43 functions.\",\"mechanism\":\"accretion around one SQLite file.\",\"refactor\":\"reader and retry policy are separable; imports only.\"},\n{\"id\":\"M5\",\"file\":\"src/tn_hivemind/core/store.py\",\"category\":\"module-too-large\",\"description\":\"654 lines: order keys (78-141), derived stamps and order (232-377), write lock (418-458), append_bundle, reads.\",\"evidence\":\"37 functions.\",\"mechanism\":\"S37 and S69 derivations added to the store.\",\"refactor\":\"derived-stamp/order code (legacy ledgers) is separable; same results.\"},\n{\"id\":\"Y1\",\"file\":\"src/tn_hivemind/core/ledger.py:500-523\",\"category\":\"layering\",\"description\":\"_thesis_dependencies hard-codes payload shapes of disposition, driver, loading, priced_state, rule_definition, rule_execution — kinds RULE_OWNERS (contracts.py:65-89) assigns to loop modules.\",\"evidence\":\"six kind branches; references only from admit (323).\",\"mechanism\":\"each new thesis-referencing kind added a branch here instead of registering.\",\"refactor\":\"a registered 'guarded_theses' aspect per kind in RULE_OWNERS; same guards computed, so same StaleHeadError behaviour; registration is a call, so imports stay downward.\"},\n{\"id\":\"Y2\",\"file\":\"src/tn_hivemind/core/contracts.py:65-89\",\"category\":\"layering\",\"description\":\"RULE_OWNERS names loop/data modules by string; a by-name upward reference, not an import (design).\",\"evidence\":\"lines cited; test_package_layers guards imports only.\",\"mechanism\":\"registration design.\",\"refactor\":\"none; fact.\"},\n{\"id\":\"Y3\",\"file\":\"src/tn_hivemind/core/ledger.py:113-114\",\"category\":\"layering\",\"description\":\"CachingStore.view_reuse and shared_view are slots for loop.view.reuse_views held on a core object.\",\"evidence\":\"10 refs in src outside core (loop/reconcile.py:194 uses reuse_views(ledger.store)).\",\"mechanism\":\"the view cache needed a per-store slot.\",\"refactor\":\"a generic per-store extension slot, or leave; only loop code moves.\"},\n{\"id\":\"Y4\",\"file\":\"src/tn_hivemind/core/store.py:319-355\",\"category\":\"layering\",\"description\":\"_legacy_passes reads the ops sidecar's run_inputs table, written by loop.reconcile (record_run_inputs, reconcile.py:298), by name.\",\"evidence\":\"lines cited; live for pre-clock ledgers (golden-v2 has no tx column).\",\"mechanism\":\"deriving known_on for old ledgers needed pass dates.\",\"refactor\":\"loop could pass the boundaries in; fact for now.\"},\n{\"id\":\"Y5\",\"file\":\"src/tn_hivemind/models/llm.py:26; transport.py:75\",\"category\":\"layering\",\"description\":\"POLICY_DIR and DEADLINE_TABLE are repository-relative paths (parents[3]) baked into library modules (AGENTS working rule 4: library code takes runtime paths as arguments).\",\"evidence\":\"grep parents[3]: 2 hits; resolve_deadline accepts table=; load_policy has no injection point and 156 refs in tests/evals/scripts.\",\"mechanism\":\"defaults chosen where the file lives.\",\"refactor\":\"a default-argument form keeps every current call identical.\"},\n{\"id\":\"Y6\",\"file\":\"src/tn_hivemind/core/parsing.py:19,161; models/embeddings.py:524\",\"category\":\"layering\",\"description\":\"The only non-stdlib imports in both packages: pypdf (optional, guarded) and numpy (lazy, in matrix).\",\"evidence\":\"grep.\",\"mechanism\":\"measured need.\",\"refactor\":\"none; fact.\"},\n{\"id\":\"P1\",\"file\":\"src/tn_hivemind/core/store.py:556-558; contracts.py:489,502,510,515,520\",\"category\":\"performance\",\"description\":\"Every dependency is fetched and JSON-decoded once in validate_dependencies' generic loop (489) and again in the kind-specific loop (a claim's passage source at 502; a thesis/evaluation/change's claims at 510, thesis at 515, evaluations at 520); each fetch is ResearchStore.get (one SQL + json.loads of the full payload). For claims the dependency is the source document (avg 6 KB, max 527 KB). The same head is also fetched twice at 544 (guards) and 551 (by_identity).\",\"evidence\":\"stage2-accept-v142: 434 bundles per loop day, avg 19.6 records, max 400 (a 400-claim bundle from one window decodes its source about 800 times, up to about 400 MB of JSON at the 527 KB maximum); claims avg 1.15 passages.\",\"mechanism\":\"the generic reference loop and the per-kind checks were written separately; no memo.\",\"refactor\":\"memoise lookup and head reads in a dict scoped to the transaction (nothing is inserted until 575, so the view is stable): identical results, no record change.\"},\n{\"id\":\"P2\",\"file\":\"src/tn_hivemind/core/store.py:304-316\",\"category\":\"performance\",\"description\":\"last_position/_next_position run SELECT MAX(tx), MAX(seq) FROM research_records on every append_bundle (531): a full table scan (no index on tx or seq).\",\"evidence\":\"EXPLAIN on stage2-accept-v142: 'SCAN research_records' (17,012 rows); 434 bundles per loop day -> about 7.4 M row visits per day, growing with the ledger.\",\"mechanism\":\"the order columns were added without an index.\",\"refactor\":\"MAX(tx) from research_transactions' PK plus an index on seq created where _ensure_order adds the columns (first admission, inside the write transaction, so 'opening never writes' holds); identical positions.\"},\n{\"id\":\"P3\",\"file\":\"src/tn_hivemind/core/ledger.py:123-139\",\"category\":\"performance\",\"description\":\"CachingStore._kind resyncs with WHERE kind=? AND rowid>? ORDER BY rowid after every data_state change; the planner walks every index entry of that kind and sorts with a temp b-tree, even for one new row.\",\"evidence\":\"EXPLAIN: 'SEARCH ... USING COVERING INDEX (kind=?)' + 'USE TEMP B-TREE FOR ORDER BY'; observation kind has 11,840 rows; every append_bundle bumps total_changes, so up to 13 kinds x 434 bundles per day resync (index entries only, no payload decode).\",\"mechanism\":\"the PK (kind, record_id, version) serves lookups, not rowid ranges.\",\"refactor\":\"an index (kind, rowid) added at first admission; identical rows.\"},\n{\"id\":\"P4\",\"file\":\"src/tn_hivemind/models/embeddings.py:363-366,392\",\"category\":\"performance\",\"description\":\"Embedder.cached selects every vector of the model (WHERE model=? AND dims=?) and filters by