re insert (see U7).\",\"evidence\":\"10 production call sites of heads('claim') alone; per-record cost.\",\"mechanism\":\"see U7.\",\"refactor\":\"minor beside P1-P5.\"},\n{\"id\":\"P8\",\"file\":\"src/tn_hivemind/core/documents.py:54-73\",\"category\":\"performance\",\"description\":\"CompactText.__init__ is a per-character Python loop over the whole document; built once per source per stage and cached (claims.py:844, relations.py:414 pass compact= into locate_quote).\",\"evidence\":\"call sites checked; no uncached construction in production.\",\"mechanism\":\"n/a.\",\"refactor\":\"none; fact.\"},\n{\"id\":\"R1\",\"file\":\"src/tn_hivemind/models/jev.py (whole); usage.py:78-80\",\"category\":\"readability\",\"description\":\"Compressed style: 26 lines without a space after commas, `if x:raise` on one line (43, 48-52, 67, 71-78, 84, 108-109); the 'jev' branch of usage_counts carries the same style.\",\"evidence\":\"grep count of no-space-after-comma lines: jev.py 26, usage.py 5.\",\"mechanism\":\"copied from another author/codebase.\",\"refactor\":\"formatting only.\"},\n{\"id\":\"R2\",\"file\":\"src/tn_hivemind/core/rules.py\",\"category\":\"readability\",\"description\":\"Double-quoted strings throughout (0 single, 79 double) while every other module uses single quotes.\",\"evidence\":\"quote count.\",\"mechanism\":\"written apart.\",\"refactor\":\"formatting only.\"},\n{\"id\":\"R3\",\"file\":\"src/tn_hivemind/core/store.py:623,644,652\",\"category\":\"readability\",\"description\":\"The only three annotated signatures (kind: str, record_id: str) in both packages.\",\"evidence\":\"grep 'def .*: str'.\",\"mechanism\":\"style drift.\",\"refactor\":\"formatting only.\"},\n{\"id\":\"R4\",\"file\":\"src/tn_hivemind/core/ledger.py:30 vs contracts.py:48\",\"category\":\"naming\",\"description\":\"Two IDENTITY_KINDS in core with different members: ledger's tuple ('entity','instrument','universe') vs contracts' frozenset {'entity','instrument'}.\",\"evidence\":\"lines cited; ledger's is used by bootstrap (369), contracts' by validate_record/manifest.\",\"mechanism\":\"bootstrap needed universes too and reused the name.\",\"refactor\":\"rename ledger's to BOOTSTRAP_KINDS; no behaviour change.\"},\n{\"id\":\"R5\",\"file\":\"src/tn_hivemind/core/parsing.py:13 vs table_evidence.py:16\",\"category\":\"naming\",\"description\":\"Two PARSER_VERSION constants ('hivemind-text-v4', 'table-evidence-v3'); both values are written into artifacts and must stay.\",\"evidence\":\"lines cited.\",\"mechanism\":\"two parsers, one name.\",\"refactor\":\"rename only (TEXT_PARSER_VERSION / TABLE_PARSER_VERSION); values untouched.\"},\n{\"id\":\"R6\",\"file\":\"src/tn_hivemind/core/contracts.py:140-181; periods.py:39,144\",\"category\":\"naming\",\"description\":\"Six 'day' helpers with four return types: canonical_day (str->str), is_day (bool), known_day/public_day (record->str), periods.day (->date), published_date (source->date).\",\"evidence\":\"periods.day imported in 10 modules, 4 as as_date.\",\"mechanism\":\"each clock rule added its reader.\",\"refactor\":\"naming only (and U15).\"},\n{\"id\":\"R7\",\"file\":\"src/tn_hivemind/core/documents.py:160\",\"category\":\"readability\",\"description\":\"locate_quote takes 10 parameters, four of them boolean profile flags (quote_terms, quote_window, quote_artifacts, quote_footers), one per claims-validator version.\",\"evidence\":\"AST; two production callers (claims.py:703, relations.py:309) pass the flags.\",\"mechanism\":\"a flag per validator version instead of a profile.\",\"refactor\":\"a frozen profile object; the branch taken per flag combination is unchanged.\"},\n{\"id\":\"R8\",\"file\":\"src/tn_hivemind/models/transport.py:5\",\"category\":\"readability\",\"description\":\"The module docstring says jev.Jev subclasses ProviderTransport; jev.py:13 declares `class Jev:` with no base.\",\"evidence\":\"lines cited.\",\"mechanism\":\"docstring written for the intended design.\",\"refactor\":\"docstring correction; free.\"},\n{\"id\":\"R9\",\"file\":\"src/tn_hivemind/core/rule_registry.py:11,181\",\"category\":\"error-handling\",\"description\":\"importlib.util.resolve_name is used with only `import importlib`; it works because site preloads importlib.util (hasattr True under python3 and python3 -I, False under python3 -S).\",\"evidence\":\"checked on Python 3.10.10.\",\"mechanism\":\"transitive import relied on.\",\"refactor\":\"`import importlib.util`; free.\"},\n{\"id\":\"R10\",\"file\":\"core/contracts.py, manifest.py, table_evidence.py, rule_registry.py, ledger.py, chunking.py\",\"category\":\"naming\",\"description\":\"Single-letter names in loops and comprehensions (p, r, d, m, g, c, s, v, k, f, h) against AGENTS' 'descriptive names'.\",\"evidence\":\"by reading: contracts.py (p, r), manifest.py (p, r, d), table_evidence.py (m, g, c, r), rule_registry.py (s, v, k, f, p), ledger.py (r, v), chunking.py (p).\",\"mechanism\":\"local shorthand.\",\"refactor\":\"mechanical rename; no behaviour change.\"},\n{\"id\":\"R11\",\"file\":\"src/tn_hivemind/core/ledger.py:61,65\",\"category\":\"naming\",\"description\":\"ref() (builds a reference) beside contracts.reference() (validates one) and record_key(); _Kind names a per-kind cache entry.\",\"evidence\":\"lines cited.\",\"mechanism\":\"short local names.\",\"refactor\":\"rename only.\"},\n{\"id\":\"R12\",\"file\":\"core/chunking.py:123; rule_registry.py:298; store.py:216; llm.py:97; usage.py:575; embeddings.py:313; documents.py:374,417\",\"category\":\"readability\",\"description\":\"Functions with more than 6 parameters: run_adaptive 9 (4 callbacks), build_definition 10, envelope 8 positional, LLM.call 7, run_model 7, Embedder.__init__ 7, _window_spans 7, windows 7.\",\"evidence\":\"AST census.\",\"mechanism\":\"option accretion.\",\"refactor\":\"keyword-only groups or small option objects; signatures only.\"},\n{\"id\":\"E1\",\"file\":\"src/tn_hivemind/core/store.py:328-337\",\"category\":\"error-handling\",\"description\":\"_legacy_passes swallows sqlite3.Error from the ops sidecar: a sidecar that exists but cannot be opened reads as 'no replay passes' and stamps derive from the known_at day (DERIVED_DAY) instead of pass dates — a silent change of derived knowledge dates on pre-clock ledgers.\",\"evidence\":\"golden-v2 (no tx column) exercises this path; 'no such table' and a corrupt file are treated alike.\",\"mechanism\":\"the derivation had to work on sidecars without run_inputs.\",\"refactor\":\"distinguishing 'no such table' from other errors would be stricter on corrupt sidecars, so it is a behaviour change there; fact.\"},\n{\"id\":\"E2\",\"file\":\"src/tn_hivemind/core/ledger.py:333-334\",\"category\":\"error-handling\",\"description\":\"admit skips the revision rule when the previous version is absent; append_bundle then refuses at store.py:553-554 ('must append consecutively'), so the skip never passes a record silently.\",\"evidence\":\"lines cited.\",\"mechanism\":\"defensive continue.\",\"refactor\":\"none; fact.\"},\n{\"id\":\"E3\",\"file\":\"src/tn_hivemind/core/archive.py:250-253\",\"category\":\"error-handling\",\"description\":\"A ValueError from public_url on a redirect target is folded into the generic 'public fetch failed; remote details omitted', losing the specific reason.\",\"evidence\":\"line 223 raises inside the try that 252 catches.\",\"mechanism\":\"one catch-all for credential safety.\",\"refactor\":\"re-raise public_url's message as FetchError (locally constructed text); changes the stored failure text, so not byte-identical for intake records; fact.\"},\n{\"id\":\"E4\",\"file\":\"src/tn_hivemind/models/embeddings.py:489-492\",\"category\":\"error-handling\",\"description\":\"OSError from archive.read_json (a missing archive object) is reported as 'invalid embedding response', conflating a missing archive file with a malformed response.\",\"evidence\":\"line 491.\",\"mechanism\":\"one catch for the decode path.\",\"refactor\":\"would change the recorded failure text; fact.\"},\n{\"id\":\"E5\",\"file\":\"src/tn_hivemind/models/embeddings.py:171\",\"category\":\"readability\",\"description\":\"Non-finite check written as `value != value or value in (inf, -inf)` where math.isfinite reads directly.\",\"evidence\":\"line cited.\",\"mechanism\":\"inline NaN idiom.\",\"refactor\":\"same truth table; free.\"}\n]\n\nPER-MODULE TABLE (lines | functions | functions > 60 lines (start, length) | functions > 6 params (count) | defined-but-unreferenced / test-only)\ncore/__init__.py | 17 | 0 | – | – | –\ncore/archive.py | 253 | 15 | fetch_public (192, 62) | – | –\ncore/chunking.py | 159 | 8 | – | run_adaptive (9) | –\ncore/contracts.py | 531 | 20 | validate_record (280, 200) | – | –\ncore/documents.py | 480 | 26 | – | locate_quote (10), _window_spans (7), windows (7) | sections.document_type never read\ncore/ledger.py | 523 | 44 | – | – | verify_read_cache test-only; ClockNotSet unused import (re-export)\ncore/manifest.py | 173 | 6 | validate_manifest (56, 118) | – | –\ncore/parsing.py | 207 | 11 | parse_bytes (134, 61) | – | –\ncore/periods.py | 185 | 14 | – | – | –\ncore/rule_registry.py | 412 | 26 | executable_references (166, 86) | build_definition (10) | –\ncore/rules.py | 200 | 10 | – | – | –\ncore/store.py | 654 | 37 | append_bundle (460, 124) | envelope (8) | list_records test-only; history_positions test-only\ncore/table_evidence.py | 314 | 9 | _parse (192, 111) | – | –\ncore/units.py | 237 | 9 | – | – | MONEY_UNITS unreferenced anywhere\nmodels/__init__.py | 13 | 0 | – | – | –\nmodels/embeddings.py | 531 | 33 | – | Embedder.__init__ (7) | – (seed_store reached from scripts/embed_store.py)\nmodels/jev.py | 110 | 5 | – | – | –\nmodels/llm.py | 178 | 15 | – | LLM.call (7) | –\nmodels/providers.py | 76 | 4 | – | – | –\nmodels/transport.py | 369 | 28 | – | – | _WatchedHTTPConnection unreachable (all endpoints https)\nmodels/truenorth.py | 138 | 6 | – | – | –\nmodels/usage.py | 614 | 43 | UsageLedger.reserve (217, 70) | run_model (7) | spent_under test-only\nTOTAL | 6374 | 369 | 9 | 10 | 1 unreferenced, 5 test-only\n\nNotes on the reference scan: _HTML.handle_startendtag and handle_data (parsing.py:112,126) showed no caller but are HTMLParser callbacks the framework invokes, so they are live; every other defined name in both packages has at least one code reference outside its definition.\n\nHot paths ranked by estimated per-pass cost (from the counted rows): P1 (dependency double-decode of source payloads on claim admission) > P2 (MAX(tx),MAX(seq) full scan per bundle, ~7.4 M row visits per loop day) > P3 (cache resync walking a kind's index per commit) > P5 (aggregate-cap scan of 77,699 calls per fresh reservation) > P4 (20-34 MB of vectors read per develop run) > P6 (window-plan linear scan, once per source per policy). All five have a behaviour-preserving form named above; P2 and P3 need an index created at first admission (never on open) to keep the \"opening a stored ledger never writes\" rule.\n\nScratch files written (temporary only): /private/tmp/claude-501/-Users-lchingen-tn-hivemind/11f89f38-a3d0-46d4-83b2-4abb9f40f537/scratchpad/census_ast.py and ast_out.txt. No repository file was changed."}},"serverClassifierRequest":"080a1cbd-5924-41fe-ae9a-ef5a10d38361","apiBlockIndex":1,"requestId":"req_011Cfxg7SQFv5bPJy69Ci1c5","attributionAgent":"general-purpose","type":"assistant","uuid":"97641b03-6ec0-49e2-9d11-ca124d11f976","timestamp":"2026-10-12T16:46:26.408Z","advisorModel":"claude-fable-5-1","effort":"xhigh","perTurnEffort":"xhigh","userType":"external","entrypoint":"cli","cwd":"/Users/lchingen/tn-hivemind","sessionId":"11f89f38-a3d0-46d4-83b2-4abb9f40f537","version":"2.1.288","gitBranch":"stage1-rework","slug":"peaceful-orbiting-diffie"}
