evals/refactor-2026-10/census/data.md:1:# Refactor census: `src/tn_hivemind/data` (20 modules, 9,851 lines)\n\nRead-only review. No file edited, no test run. Instruments: AST statistics, pyflakes, a token-based cross-reference over every `.py`/`.sh` under `src`, `tests`, `evals`, `scripts` (731 files), difflib overlap on suspected copies, and call-count harnesses run on stored data only (the gate's `golden-offline.sqlite3` opened read-only, `prices-2026-10-09.json`, `consensus-2026-09-26.json`, the GOOG v7 catalog snapshot).\n\n## Summary: the five mechanisms behind most findings\n\n1. **Parallel pipelines copied, not shared (duplication).** `claims`↔`relations` (window-extraction driver, `verify`, record builders, `profile_for`), `news`↔`transcripts` (acquire→derive→review→admit chain), the three MCP transports inside `intake.acquire`, `catalog.fetch`↔`fetch_filing_texts`, `observe.run`↔`observe._refusals`, `observe.catalog_index`↔`load_snapshots`. Each second pipeline was started from a copy of the first and then diverged by a few parameters. All are byte-identical-output refactors if the shared driver takes the differing strings (log prefixes, reviewer/note, stage names) as arguments.\n2. **Small helpers and tables re-implemented per module instead of living in `core`.** Month tables (4 copies in `data`, one of them identical to `core.periods.MONTHS`), the CJK regex (2 in `data`, 7 in `src`), the repo-root path (3 in `data`, 10 in `src`), ISO-time parsing (`observations._parse_time`/`_iso` vs `desk.instant`/`iso` vs `catalog._moment_key`), head-folding over record lists (3 copies in `data` + `core.ledger.Ledger.heads`), closes parsing (`marks` vs `desk`), `desk._median` vs `statistics.median`, the ttm/ytd regex (`kpi_series` vs `stated_figures`), derivation formula strings (`catalog` inline ×5 vs `observations.FORMULAS`). A few near-copies have *diverged* (scale words, legal-suffix sets) and are not safe to merge without proof.\n3. **Accretion by version flags and record fields (long signatures, lazy imports, over-public constants).** `claims.verify` carries 7 booleans that mirror the `VALIDATORS` dict (16 parameters); `relations.verify` 4; `data_needs.classify`/`_line_path` 11; `observations.make_observation` 15. Seven lazy imports in `data_needs`/`observe` guard no cycle (verified: `core.contracts`, `core.periods`, `models.truenorth` import nothing from `data`). 197 public (no underscore) module-level names are referenced only inside their own module (desk 47, observations 29, relations 22, data_needs 18, catalog 14...).\n4. **Stateless functions re-read whole record kinds per call (performance).** Measured on the golden ledger: one `kpi_series()` call = 5 full-kind store reads (4,843 records), one `stated_kpis.kpi_observations()` = 4 reads (4,457 records), one `observe.catalog_lines()` reads all 11,840 observations of every entity to serve one entity (called twice per formation call), one `desk()` makes 239 `Ledger.quarters` + 60 `latest_instant` scans and 13,359 `_parse_time` calls for only 16 month ends (scales linearly with the prices history), `claims.verify` re-normalizes the whole source text (up to 519 KB) per claim that carries a name-like number. None of these change outputs; indexes/memos per call site would remove them.\n5. **The module is the stage (module-too-large).** `desk.py` 1,953, `observations.py` 1,198, `data_needs.py` 1,030, `claims.py` 926, `catalog.py` 902 each hold 4–6 concerns already separated by `# ----` banners; the longest functions (`_core_blocks` 184, `build_relationships` 137, `acquire` 125, `desk` 122, `extract_sources` 116, `registry_problems` 113, `extract_mentions` 107, `gap_report` 106) are the banner sections that were never split. Pure moves with re-exports preserve every request, log line and record.\n\nWhat the guards pin (so every \"possible\" below assumes it): request text (`claims.build_user`, `claims.entity_block`, `desk.render`), log lines (`extract:`, `relations:`, `observe:`, `news:`, `transcripts:`, the `FAILED:`/`COVERAGE GAP` lines), record payload contents and key order, `short_hash` identity dicts, `ledger.reject` stage names, policy/prompt sha256s.\n\n## Findings (JSON)\n\n```json\n[\n{\"id\":1,\"file\":\"src/tn_hivemind/data/claims.py:811-926 and relations.py:396-502\",\"category\":\"duplication\",\"description\":\"The windowed extraction driver (plan windows per source, log line, run closure, run_adaptive wiring with on_split/on_gap, failed/gap window recording, per-item verify→reject→record, record_window done) is written twice.\",\"evidence\":\"difflib: 40 identical stripped lines of 110/102; same blocks claims 833-849/863-893/901-908/916-921 vs relations 412-418/435-460/475-482/497-499; both import run_adaptive, plan_windows, CompactText.\",\"mechanism\":\"relations.py was started from a copy of claims.py (copy).\",\"refactor\":\"Possible: one driver taking (stage name, log prefix, schema, build_user, verify, make_record, dedupe) as callables; log strings and reject stage names passed verbatim so lines stay byte-identical.\"},\n{\"id\":2,\"file\":\"src/tn_hivemind/data/claims.py:694-714 and relations.py:299-320\",\"category\":\"duplication\",\"description\":\"The first half of both verify functions (statement_too_short, statement_not_english, quote_missing, locate_quote, quote_too_long, context locate) is the same code with two literal differences (context max 400 vs 600; claims has `covered`).\",\"evidence\":\"20 identical stripped lines of 74/52; identical reason strings.\",\"mechanism\":\"copy.\",\"refactor\":\"Possible: `_locate_item(item, text, window, compact, *, context_max, covered, **flags)` returning (statement, span, context) or reason; same reason strings.\"},\n{\"id\":3,\"file\":\"src/tn_hivemind/data/claims.py:748-781 and relations.py:350-383\",\"category\":\"duplication\",\"description\":\"Record builders share the passages construction (claims 756-759 = relations 356-359 verbatim) and the payload skeleton (schema_version, synthetic, statement, attribution, modality, subject_refs, other_subjects, passages, claim_kind, measurements, period, materiality, topics, section, assessment_status, provenance, extraction).\",\"evidence\":\"13 identical stripped lines of 34/34; 17 shared payload keys in the same order.\",\"mechanism\":\"copy.\",\"refactor\":\"Possible for the passages helper outright; the skeleton only if key order is preserved (stored JSON).\"},\n{\"id\":4,\"file\":\"src/tn_hivemind/data/news.py:147-157 and transcripts.py:76-86\",\"category\":\"duplication\",\"description\":\"The acquire→derive→rule-review→admit chain with its three held-item branches is the same in both intakes; only the held id key (story_id vs id), reviewer and note differ.\",\"evidence\":\"9 identical stripped lines of 23/20; identical control flow and `held.append({... 'stage': 'acquire'|'derive' ...})` shapes.\",\"mechanism\":\"copy (transcripts intake modelled on news intake).\",\"refactor\":\"Possible: `intake.admit_document(archive, store, client, document, route, *, reviewer, note)` → (result | None, held reason); callers keep their log line and id key.\"},\n{\"id\":5,\"file\":\"src/tn_hivemind/data/intake.py:49-54, 74-79, 98-105\",\"category\":\"duplication\",\"description\":\"Three MCP transport branches repeat the receipt bookkeeping (archive.put(json_bytes(result)), the `response` dict with representation/received_at/provider/bytes, tool_payload, provider_status).\",\"evidence\":\"3× the same 6-line block inside one 125-line function (acquire, lines 18-142).\",\"mechanism\":\"accretion: news and transcript transports were added beside the filing transport by copying its block.\",\"refactor\":\"Possible: `_mcp_receipt(receipt, archive, result)` returning the payload; dict keys/order unchanged.\"},\n{\"id\":6,\"file\":\"src/tn_hivemind/data/catalog.py:133-143 and 160-171\",\"category\":\"duplication\",\"description\":\"fetch and fetch_filing_texts record a call identically (try/except Exception → failed record with truncated error; else status by payload['status'] with the same 'provider status …' error text).\",\"evidence\":\"10 identical stripped lines of 20/23; two `noqa: BLE001` excepts.\",\"mechanism\":\"copy when filing texts were added to the fetch plan.\",\"refactor\":\"Possible: `_record_call(record, call)` shared by both; identical dict shapes.\"},\n{\"id\":7,\"file\":\"src/tn_hivemind/data/observe.py:342-376 and 395-468\",\"category\":\"duplication\",\"description\":\"run and _refusals walk the same pending snapshot units then release units, threading heads/held and building records the same way; one admits, the other checks.\",\"evidence\":\"_refusals duplicates run's unit iteration (snapshot_unit/release_unit, _entity_ref, parse_table_evidence, release_cell_observations, refuse_changed_content loop) with a check sink; 10 identical stripped lines, 70-line function.\",\"mechanism\":\"the preflight (refusals) was added as a copy of run with a different sink.\",\"refactor\":\"Possible with care: a unit iterator yielding (unit id, kind, snapshot, build-records thunk) consumed by both; the order and the heads/held threading must stay exactly as in run.\"},\n{\"id\":8,\"file\":\"src/tn_hivemind/data/observe.py:143-166 and 173-187\",\"category\":\"duplication\",\"description\":\"catalog_index and load_snapshots both glob `*-catalog.json`, compute the verdict key, verify (memoized) and sort by the same key; run() calls both in sequence.\",\"evidence\":\"9 identical stripped lines; same sort key tuple at 165 and 186.\",\"mechanism\":\"catalog_index was added later as a facts-only fast path beside the full loader.\",\"refactor\":\"Possible: load_snapshots = parse the paths catalog_index returns (same verdict memo, same order).\"},\n{\"id\":9,\"file\":\"src/tn_hivemind/data/marks.py:50-59,62-73 and desk.py:160-168,176-179\",\"category\":\"duplication\",\"description\":\"Two parsers of the prices snapshot's closes and two 'last close on or before' rules (linear scan vs bisect).\",\"evidence\":\"closes_from_snapshot/close_on vs entity_closes/close_on_or_before; both read entities[id].closes as pairs or {date, close}; both called from loop and readmodel.\",\"mechanism\":\"desk.py reimplemented marks' reader rather than importing it.\",\"refactor\":\"Possible with care: the filters differ on malformed sessions (`day(when) is not None` vs `len(str(session)) >= 10` + `[:10]`); identical for the ISO dates refresh_events writes.\"},\n{\"id\":10,\"file\":\"src/tn_hivemind/data/data_needs.py:746-751, 779-783; kpi_series.py:49-53\",\"category\":\"duplication\",\"description\":\"Head folding over a record list ('keep the highest version per (kind,id), first-seen order') is written three times in the package (plus core.ledger.Ledger.heads 271-283 and loop/factor_decide 475-478).\",\"evidence\":\"grep: 3 copies of the `if key not in heads or heads[key]['version'] < …` loop in data.\",\"mechanism\":\"no core helper exists; each reader wrote its own.\",\"refactor\":\"Possible: `core.ledger.heads_of(records)`; insertion order and highest-version semantics are identical in all copies.\"},\n{\"id\":11,\"file\":\"src/tn_hivemind/data/data_needs.py:743 vs 772\",\"category\":\"readability\",\"description\":\"The two entry paths of _records read different kind sets: load_records reads sorted(contracts.KINDS); the Ledger-like path reads a hard-coded 7-kind tuple (no claim, relationship, change…).\",\"evidence\":\"lines 743 and 772.\",\"mechanism\":\"accretion: the Ledger path was added with the kinds the gap report needed at the time.\",\"refactor\":\"Behaviour-preserving only as documentation; aligning the kind sets changes what the report scans (check gap_report consumers first).\"},\n{\"id\":12,\"file\":\"src/tn_hivemind/data/observations.py:112-129 and desk.py:122-139 (also catalog.py:118-119, 333-338; news.py:55-57)\",\"category\":\"duplication\",\"description\":\"Five ISO-time helpers: _parse_time/_iso (observations), instant/iso (desk, adds the compact run-id form and the 10-char → end-of-day rule that observations.available_by applies at line 141), catalog.utc_now and _moment_key, news.published_iso; core.archive.now exists.\",\"evidence\":\"grep over `def (utc_now|now|iso|_iso|published_iso|instant|_parse_time|_moment_key)` in src: 14 definitions, 5 in data.\",\"mechanism\":\"no `core` time module; each stage wrote the parser it needed.\",\"refactor\":\"Possible: one core helper `instant(value, precision)`; desk.instant ≡ _parse_time(value, 'date' if len==10 else 'second') plus the compact form; outputs identical for the inputs callers pass.\"},\n{\"id\":13,\"file\":\"src/tn_hivemind/data/claims.py:43-44,120-121,203; filing_tables.py:53-54; stated_figures.py:76-78; desk.py:935\",\"category\":\"duplication\",\"description\":\"Four month tables in data: claims._MONTHS (full+3-letter) equals core.periods.MONTHS (periods.py:17-18) exactly; filing_tables.MONTHS, stated_figures._MONTHS and desk._MONTH_NUMBERS are the same full-name-only table (used in regex alternations).\",\"evidence\":\"grep across src: 6 month tables (data 4, core 1, loop 1).\",\"mechanism\":\"missing shared table; each parser built its own.\",\"refactor\":\"Possible: claims imports core.periods.MONTHS; the three full-name copies share one constant with Jan..Dec insertion order (regex alternations depend on order, which all copies share).\"},\n{\"id\":14,\"file\":\"src/tn_hivemind/data/claims.py:116 and data_needs.py:89\",\"category\":\"duplication\",\"description\":\"Identical CJK regex literal (7 copies across src: 2 in data, 5 in loop).\",\"evidence\":\"grep -F of the character class: 7 hits.\",\"mechanism\":\"copied per module that validates English text.\",\"refactor\":\"Possible: one `core` constant; identical pattern.\"},\n{\"id\":15,\"file\":\"src/tn_hivemind/data/kpi_series.py:60 and stated_figures.py:91\",\"category\":\"duplication\",\"description\":\"The same 'not one period' regex (ttm|trailing|ytd|…|half) inline in _period_key and as stated_figures._NOT_ONE_PERIOD; kpi_series already imports from stated_figures.\",\"evidence\":\"grep: 2 identical patterns.\",\"mechanism\":\"copy.\",\"refactor\":\"Possible: import the constant.\"},\n{\"id\":16,\"file\":\"src/tn_hivemind/data/catalog.py:470,509,547,566,585 vs observations.py:301-305 (and kpi_series.py:203)\",\"category\":\"duplication\",\"description\":\"Derivation formula strings are literals in catalog._derive/_derive_q4_rates and again in observations.FORMULAS; the validator recomputes against the latter.\",\"evidence\":\"5 inline literals + 1 table; the method names also appear in observations.DERIVED_METHODS (90-91) and _compute (288-298).\",\"mechanism\":\"observations was written against catalog's output rather than sharing its table (catalog is below observations in the intra-package import order, so the table belongs in catalog).\",\"refactor\":\"Possible: move FORMULAS to catalog (or catalog_names) and import it in observations; same strings.\"},\n{\"id\":17,\"file\":\"src/tn_hivemind/data/relations.py:38, claims.py:27, data_needs.py:57\",\"category\":\"duplication\",\"description\":\"Three independent `Path(__file__).resolve().parents[3]` repo-root computations (10 across src; cli.runtime.REPOSITORY exists but is in the top layer).\",\"evidence\":\"grep parents[3]: 10 hits.\",\"mechanism\":\"no core path constant.\",\"refactor\":\"Possible: `core.paths.REPOSITORY`; same resolved path.\"},\n{\"id\":18,\"file\":\"src/tn_hivemind/data/desk.py:718-723\",\"category\":\"duplication\",\"description\":\"desk._median re-implements statistics.median (observations.py uses statistics.median at 1023/1041/1055).\",\"evidence\":\"identical semantics for non-empty lists; callers already guard emptiness (769, 871) except `_median(others) or 0.0` at 769 which needs `if others`.\",\"mechanism\":\"local re-implementation.\",\"refactor\":\"Possible with the one guard added.\"},\n{\"id\":19,\"file\":\"src/tn_hivemind/data/desk.py:606-608, 808-809, 1254\",\"category\":\"duplication\",\"description\":\"Three FY-label helpers in one module: _label_key (regex → tuple or None), _label (tuple → 'FY%d Q%d'), and the key_of lambda in press_consensus (same regex, raises on mismatch); also months_back/months_later (152-154, 726-728).\",\"evidence\":\"lines cited; noqa E731 on the lambda.\",\"mechanism\":\"accretion as the press and v5 blocks were appended.\",\"refactor\":\"Possible: key_of → _label_key where the input is known to match (upcoming/fiscal_quarter labels are produced by _label).\"},\n{\"id\":20,\"file\":\"src/tn_hivemind/data/stated_figures.py:34-35 vs desk.py:932-933; relations.py:57-58 vs desk.py:1139-1140\",\"category\":\"duplication\",\"description\":\"Near-copies that have diverged: scale words (stated has 'tn' and 'thousand', desk has 't' and no 'thousand'; 3 more in loop/readmodel) and legal-suffix sets (relations has llc/pbc/holding/lp/llp; the strip loops differ: `len>1` vs pop-all).\",\"evidence\":\"grep: 5 scale tables and 2 suffix sets in src.\",\"mechanism\":\"copied then edited independently.\",\"refactor\":\"Not behaviour-preserving to merge; census only (a merge needs the union proven on stored statements/headlines).\"},\n{\"id\":21,\"file\":\"src/tn_hivemind/data/kpi_series.py:145-219 (stated_measurements 71-108, calendar 116-124)\",\"category\":\"performance\",\"description\":\"One kpi_series call re-reads whole record kinds five times: heads_at(entity) in kpi_series, heads_at(source) in calendar, then stated_measurements recomputes heads_at(entity), known_at(source), heads_at(claim).\",\"evidence\":\"Measured on the golden ledger (store path): record_snapshot(entity)×2, (source)×2, (claim)×1 = 4,843 records read per call, 0.07 s; debates/factor_calls.py:282 calls it once per shown KPI key per formation call; on the View path each read iterates every record of every kind (by_key.values(), ~17k records) and filters by kind.\",\"mechanism\":\"design choice: each function derives its own heads from the ledger rather than receiving them.\",\"refactor\":\"Possible: compute (entities, sources, claims) heads once per (ledger, as_of) and pass them down; same records, same order (heads_at sorts by admission_key).\"},\n{\"id\":22,\"file\":\"src/tn_hivemind/data/stated_kpis.py:20-55\",\"category\":\"performance\",\"description\":\"kpi_observations repeats the same kind reads per entity per day (calendar + stated_measurements) and calls statement_figures per measurement.\",\"evidence\":\"Measured: 4 kind reads, 4,457 records read per call (3 keys), loop/factor_stage.py:112 once per entity per loop day.\",\"mechanism\":\"same as #21.\",\"refactor\":\"Same as #21.\"},\n{\"id\":23,\"file\":\"src/tn_hivemind/data/observe.py:517-570\",\"category\":\"performance\",\"description\":\"catalog_lines reads every observation of every entity (ledger.records('observation')) and filters by entity inside the loop; the caller passes one entity.\",\"evidence\":\"Measured: 11,840 records read per call, 0.14 s, 58 lines returned; call sites debates/factor_calls.py:182 and :272 (twice per formation call when no catalog option), compose.py:553, loop/ideas.py:472, loop/decide_request.py:474 (cached per entity+month).\",\"mechanism\":\"a stateless reader over the whole kind; the store has no per-entity read.\",\"refactor\":\"Possible: accept an entity-filtered observation list (the `observations=` parameter already exists) and let callers index once per pass; output identical.\"},\n{\"id\":24,\"file\":\"src/tn_hivemind/data/desk.py:219-253 (Ledger.quarters/latest_instant), 518, 750-797, 906-916\",\"category\":\"performance\",\"description\":\"Ledger.quarters re-sorts and re-parses the same payloads for every (line, cutoff): sort key calls effective_available per payload, then available_by parses again; multiples_point per month end calls quarter_table (7 lines) + valuation_at (3 quarters + 3 latest_instant); desk() line 518 calls gaap_flags without a table for every record row (4 quarters each, all rows not just RECORD_PRINTS).\",\"evidence\":\"Measured on stored inputs (176 desk-line observations, 350 known closes, 16 month ends, 8 printed rows): 239 Ledger.quarters + 60 latest_instant scans over 5,455 payloads, 13,359 _parse_time, 9,338 effective_available, 329 gaap_flags, 20 valuation_at, 17 multiples_point; 0.02 s. Linear in month ends: a 10-year prices snapshot (~120 month ends) ⇒ ~100k parses per desk. Per pass: one desk per (entity, date) in review (memoized loop/review.py:170-176) and one per formation call (factor_calls.py:267, exposure.py:653, debates/loop.py:139, 1230).\",\"mechanism\":\"design choice: the per-entity index stores raw payloads and recomputes availability per query.\",\"refactor\":\"Possible: parse effective_available once in Ledger.__init__ and keep per-line lists sorted; pass the quarter_table into gaap_flags at line 518; identical values.\"},\n{\"id\":25,\"file\":\"src/tn_hivemind/data/claims.py:419-423, 456, 485, 720-721\",\"category\":\"performance\",\"description\":\"ungrounded_numbers_by_role's `_in_document` cache is a per-call dict, so each claim whose number reads as a name re-normalizes the whole source (`' '.join(document().lower().split())`) after the lambda at 721 has already built `text + '\\\\n' + title` (a full copy).\",\"evidence\":\"golden ledger: largest source text 519,272 chars; windows per 10-K ≈ text/16,000 ≈ 33, up to 80 claims each (SCHEMA maxItems); contexts[source['id']] (844) already holds a per-source CompactText that could carry the normalized text.\",\"mechanism\":\"the v3 validator was added inside verify without a per-source memo.\",\"refactor\":\"Possible: memoize the normalized document per source id (e.g. on the CompactText held in contexts) and pass it through; same string, same answers.\"},\n{\"id\":26,\"file\":\"src/tn_hivemind/data/claims.py:784-808\",\"category\":\"performance\",\"description\":\"drop_overlapping_duplicates is O(n²) per window and recomputes numbers(q['statement']) for the kept record inside the inner loop (line 802) although key_numbers is computed once per record.\",\"evidence\":\"n ≤ 80 per window ⇒ ≤ 6,400 regex scans per window; windows per pass = windows run.\",\"mechanism\":\"accretion.\",\"refactor\":\"Possible: precompute numbers per record once; same comparisons, same kept list.\"},\n{\"id\":27,\"file\":\"src/tn_hivemind/data/observations.py:380-423, 375-377 (entry_for catalog.py:845-856)\",\"category\":\"performance\",\"description\":\"bind_row loops every snapshot line (GOOG v7: 450 lines) for each release row and, per resolved cell, scans the line's history linearly through entry_for.\",\"evidence\":\"estimate per release: rows (100-300) × 450 lines × 4-6 cells × ~10 history entries ≈ 2-8M entry visits; runs once per pending release unit in observe.run (loop/reconcile.py:242) and again in observe.refusals (cli/daily.py:857 preflight) for units still pending.\",\"mechanism\":\"design choice: binding by numbers over the whole catalog, with no (unit, period) index.\",\"refactor\":\"Possible: pre-index provider level lines by (unit, kind, fiscal_year, fiscal_quarter) → entries once per snapshot; identical matches and tie-breaks if the candidate order is kept as snapshot['lines'] order.\"},\n{\"id\":28,\"file\":\"src/tn_hivemind/data/catalog.py:619-677 (_agreement 598-616), 420-443, 703-727, 739-758\",\"category\":\"performance\",\"description\":\"collapse_duplicates is O(n²) over ~190 provider+company candidates with _agreement rebuilding two _by_fiscal_period dicts per pair inside a `while merged` repeat; _rate_operands is O(levels²) per company margin line; _refresh_availability and _drop_unresolved rebuild a 4,511-entry index on every fixpoint iteration.\",\"evidence\":\"GOOG v7 snapshot: 450 lines, 4,511 history entries, 66 provider + 126 company lines ⇒ ~18k _agreement calls per outer pass. Runs once per snapshot per process (build_snapshot at fetch; verify_snapshot memoized by content in observe._verify), so not a per-pass path.\",\"mechanism\":\"design choice: pairwise agreement without a period index.\",\"refactor\":\"Possible (memoize _by_fiscal_period per line id within one collapse, build `held` incrementally); snapshot_id and lines must stay identical, which the memo preserves.\"},\n{\"id\":29,\"file\":\"src/tn_hivemind/data/kpi_series.py:38-44\",\"category\":\"performance\",\"description\":\"known_at re-filters by known_on after store.record_snapshot already applied as_of, parsing each record's known_on twice (day() ×2).\",\"evidence\":\"lines 41 and 44.\",\"mechanism\":\"the View path (no as_of cut) and the store path share one filter.\",\"refactor\":\"Possible: parse once; same set.\"},\n{\"id\":30,\"file\":\"src/tn_hivemind/data/data_needs.py:998-1004, 1010-1011\",\"category\":\"performance\",\"description\":\"gap_report's driver rows and by_company summary rescan all check rows per driver / per company (O(drivers × rows)).\",\"evidence\":\"one-off CLI (data-gaps) and read model; rows = every check of every thesis.\",\"mechanism\":\"accretion.\",\"refactor\":\"Possible: group rows once; same counts.\"},\n{\"id\":31,\"file\":\"src/tn_hivemind/data/desk.py:1824-1933\",\"category\":\"layering\",\"description\":\"Four loaders hand-write SQL against research_records (table and column names, json_extract paths) instead of core.store (which data_needs.load_records uses at 735-751); load_observations (1826-1827) does not even use the _read_only helper defined at 1839.\",\"evidence\":\"4 sqlite3.connect sites; schema knowledge duplicated outside core.store.\",\"mechanism\":\"desk was built as a standalone script-style reader.\",\"refactor\":\"Possible for _read_only reuse now; moving to ResearchStore.record_snapshot would read whole kinds (observation 11,840) instead of the entity's 10 lines, so that part is a performance trade, not a pure move.\"},\n{\"id\":32,\"file\":\"src/tn_hivemind/data/desk.py:1943-1953\",\"category\":\"error-handling\",\"description\":\"snapshot_entity_id raises SystemExit from library code (callers: evals/formation-v1/bench.py:182, two tests).\",\"evidence\":\"line 1953.\",\"mechanism\":\"a CLI concern placed in the data layer.\",\"refactor\":\"Not strictly behaviour-preserving (exception type seen by tests changes); census only.\"},\n{\"id\":33,\"file\":\"src/tn_hivemind/data/data_needs.py:117, 536, 577, 830, 948; observe.py:396-397\",\"category\":\"readability\",\"description\":\"Seven function-local imports guard no cycle: core.periods is already imported at data_needs top (54); observations imports core.contracts at its top (72) and nothing in core/models imports data (grep: 0 hits); models.truenorth is pure urllib.\",\"evidence\":\"grep of lazy imports; cycle check.\",\"mechanism\":\"accretion from an earlier module layout.\",\"refactor\":\"Possible: hoist to module top; import order within the package stays acyclic (catalog_names ← catalog/filing_tables/stated_figures ← kpi_series ← observations ← observe/desk/stated_kpis/data_needs).\"},\n{\"id\":34,\"file\":\"src/tn_hivemind/data/claims.py:39-41; relations.py:230-231, 580-581\",\"category\":\"readability\",\"description\":\"Import-time file I/O: four extraction prompts and two relations prompts are read and hashed when the package imports (relations is imported for JevTagger/registry use too).\",\"evidence\":\"PROMPTS dict comprehension at import; PROMPT/ADJUDICATE_PROMPT read_text at import.\",\"mechanism\":\"prompt sha256 as a module constant.\",\"refactor\":\"Possible (lazy, cached loader returning the same text/sha); every policy sha stays identical.\"},\n{\"id\":35,\"file\":\"src/tn_hivemind/data/claims.py:668-670; relations.py:296-297\",\"category\":\"readability\",\"description\":\"verify takes 16 parameters (claims) / 11 (relations): seven/four booleans that are exactly the keys of VALIDATORS; extract_sources unpacks the profile dict into them (896-900) and relations passes **profile.\",\"evidence\":\"AST: claims.verify 16 params; VALIDATORS at 56-62 and 234-236.\",\"mechanism\":\"accretion: one flag per validator version.\",\"refactor\":\"Possible: pass the profile dict (defaults as today); same checks in the same order.\"},\n{\"id\":36,\"file\":\"src/tn_hivemind/data/observations.py:153-154; data_needs.py:488-489, 557-558, 618-619, 338-339; relations.py:148, 172, 396-397, 672-673; catalog.py:269; filing_tables.py:352; news.py:71\",\"category\":\"readability\",\"description\":\"Functions with more than six parameters (full list in the table): make_observation 15, classify 11, _line_path 11, _result 10, extract_mentions 10, make_need 9, extract_sources 9, desk 9, claim_record 8, mention_record 8, derived_observation 8, kill_line_check 8, _join_no_data 8, classify_for_projection 8, filing_entries 8, Resolver._new 8, build_relationships 8, build_user 7, _filing_rows 7, Resolver.resolve 7, discover 7, _Builder.add 7.\",\"evidence\":\"AST count of positional+keyword parameters.\",\"mechanism\":\"record fields and run-time options passed one by one.\",\"refactor\":\"Possible where a context object already exists (registry/as_of/fye_month/observations/answers in data_needs; policy_id/result/window in record builders); keyword-only signatures keep call sites unchanged.\"},\n{\"id\":37,\"file\":\"src/tn_hivemind/data/desk.py:1395-1578\",\"category\":\"long-function\",\"description\":\"_core_blocks (184 lines) renders six text blocks in one function while the history blocks each have their own function (_multiples_lines 1616, _base_rate_lines 1715, _press_lines 1753, _current_year_lines 1372).\",\"evidence\":\"AST: longest function in the package; the inconsistent structure is visible at 1580-1818.\",\"mechanism\":\"the v1 desk text was one function; later blocks were added as functions.\",\"refactor\":\"Possible: one function per block returning (key, lines); the joined text is unchanged.\"},\n{\"id\":38,\"file\":\"src/tn_hivemind/data/desk.py (1,953 lines)\",\"category\":\"module-too-