evals/pm-protocol-v1/runs/vq5c-paired/aapl-2026-09-26/packet-1/brief-1.md:227:- scenarios: deciding metric: FY2026 revenue growth over FY2025; unit: percent; bull: outcome: FY2026 growth reaches 15.7% as the iPhone cycle and the usual beat run stronger than the anchor assumes.; value: 15.7; probability: 0.25; base: outcome: FY2026 growth is 14.4%; the guided Q4 deceleration offsets part, but not all, of Q1–Q3 strength.; value: 14.4; probability: 0.5; bear: outcome: FY2026 growth falls to 13.3% as Q4 revenue undershoots the anchor amid weaker demand and cost-related pricing pressure.; value: 13.3; probability: 0.25; skew: 1.18; expected value: 14.45; anchor: 14.9; anchor basis: consensus_build, a build from the reported quarters, the next quarter at its anchor and any later quarter at an assumed growth, not a published consensus; gap vs anchor: -0.0302; path metric: revenue_growth_fy1
evals/pm-protocol-v1/runs/run11-own-date/amzn-2026-08-06/packet-1/brief-1.md:125:- [A3] Market value added by the recent moves (at 10,756M shares): 1m +$302B; 3m -$29B.
evals/pm-protocol-v1/runs/run11-own-date/amzn-2026-08-06/packet-1/brief-1.md:214:- why it moves the stock: The price discounts the fade, not durability. The market is reacting to the Q2 report (revenue $200.61B, +1.8% over the pre-print consensus [R1]): +15.3% the next session [Y1], about $302B of market value in a month [A3]. Yet that only returned the normalized P/E to 35.7x, near its 35.5x median [M2]; over trailing revenue growth of +15.8% [M4] it is about 2.26 (arithmetic), below 3.04-3.55 at the 2025-04 to 2025-09 month ends, when GAAP and normalized P/E were equal [M6]. Base rate: revenue beat 8 of 8 (median +1.1% [A4]) and finished above the guide range 2 of 2 [B1]; next-session reactions 3 up, 3 down [Y9], context only.
evals/pm-protocol-v1/runs/run11-own-date/amzn-2026-08-06/packet-1/brief-1.md:225:- debate: question: Is the acceleration of revenue growth to +19.6% YoY in FY2026 Q2 [A5] durable, or does it fade to the +10.7% the Q3 guide midpoint implies (arithmetic on [B2], [R4])?; value driver: Consolidated revenue growth, the line the multiple is paid on; each point of Q3 YoY growth is about $1.8B of revenue (1% of $180.17B [R4], arithmetic), and the stock added about $302B of market value in the month that included the Q2 report [A3]; rank: 1
