evals/pm-protocol-v1/runs/run11-own-date/amzn-2026-08-06/packet-1/brief-2.md:125:- [A3] Market value added by the recent moves (at 10,756M shares): 1m +$302B; 3m -$29B.
evals/pm-protocol-v1/runs/run11-own-date/amzn-2026-08-06/packet-1/brief-2.md:215:- bear case: The strongest bear case is that the normalized 35.7x trailing P/E requires 25.0% annual EPS growth for five years to an 18x exit, while the desk’s anchored EPS path is only 8.3% [M2][A9][A8]. The investment burden is already visible: TTM free cash flow is -$11.625B, TTM capex is $173.028B, and Amazon guided to approximately $220B of cash capex in 2026 [L14][L11]. Revenue and AWS are accelerating, but the price has advanced 11.5% in one month and added about $302B of market value; the bear argues those strong prints do not yet establish the much longer EPS growth duration embedded in the price [P2][A3][L2][L19].
