   641	## 7. Where Jev fits
   642	
   643	**What Jev is.** Jev (`jev-1.13.0`, TypeSafe) returns typed `choice` or `score`
   644	answers with calibrated probabilities and generates no text.
   645	- **Price:** $0.042 per million input tokens and nothing for output. Luna costs
   646	  $0.10–0.125 per million input tokens plus $0.50 per million output.
   647	- **Measured on our evidence relations:** Jev alone 81.2%, the Jev-first
   648	  cascade 88.4% on test, Luna alone 85.8%.
   649	- **Vendor claims (unverified):** 70–500 ms latency, and "zero hallucination",
   650	  which only means answers match the schema.
   651	
   652	| Task | Jev question | Fit | Fallback / guard |
   653	| --- | --- | --- | --- |
   654	| Relation type and direction of a counterparty mention | choice over the roles in §4.2, plus "not a firm-to-firm relation" | Good: closed set; reversed direction and product-vs-company confusion are classification errors | Luna's extraction label is primary; a confident disagreement means Luna decides or the item is held for review |
   655	| Channel | choice over ~13 channels | Good | Luna label |
   656	| Kind of shock | choice: demand, supply/capacity, input price, product/technology, regulatory, financial, other | Good; drives the direction rule | Routing uses only the named/declared routes when uncertain |
   657	| Dependency level and specificity from cue language | score | Good | `unknown` below the confidence threshold |
   658	| Which entity a name refers to | choice over registry candidates plus "none" | Good: a finite candidate list | The alias table is tried first; "none" creates a reference-only entity; Jev never makes the final merge of two existing entities |
   659	| Cross-company routing gate | choice: bears on / does not bear on the premise | Good for volume (claims × premises) | Threshold tuned for recall; Luna route call below it |
   660	| Evidence judgment | existing cascade (0.95) | Measured | Luna |
   661	| Finding names or spans; writing reasons, dates or periods; merging or ending links; invalidation | — | Not suitable: needs generation, long context or authority | Luna and Python only |
   662	
   663	Jev and Luna come from different vendors, so their disagreement is a useful
   664	flag. Their agreement is still two models agreeing, not independent
   665	corroboration. The vendor calibrates Jev's probabilities; we trust them only
   666	after measuring them on dev. No Jev task is switched on before that comparison.
   667	
   668	## 8. Evaluation (bench-v1 extension, frozen before code)
   669	
