    30	What this says for our two questions. Membership ("does this question belong to this matter?") is the shape Jev did well on: a closed set, one quote, no generation. Identity ("is this the same quantity?") is the shape it did badly on alone (74% on role, a question that also turns on fine distinctions), so Jev is the check and the key gate plus the matching call stay the judge, as the old cascade did. Both come with calibrated probabilities, which a cross-encoder's sigmoid does not give; the old repository trusted them only after measuring them on dev, and so do we.
